\par\par \b \uc2 INTERVIEW-Indonesia tinplate maker sees higher 2012 capacity\b0\par\par\uc2 738 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Oktober 2011\par 12:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited \par \par \uc2 * Output seen lower this year but capacity boost in 2012\par \par \uc2 * Euro zone debt to ease, tin at $18,000-$24,000/T range in 2012\par \par \uc2 * Indonesian rupiah below 9,000 best for foreign investors\par \par \uc2 By Michael Taylor\par \par \uc2 JAKARTA, Oct 11 (Reuters) - Output at Indonesia's only tinplate producer will slip almost 10 percent this year as improvement works begin this month, in a project that will help ramp up capacity for 2012 by nearly a quarter, a director at the firm said on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 PT Pelat Timah Nusantara\uc2  Tbk , also known as \uc2 PT Latinusa Tbk\uc2 , produced 110,000 tonnes of tinplate last year and this is forecast to fall to 100,000 tonnes in 2011, Hideyuki Iwasaki, deputy of finance director, told Reuters.\par \par \uc2 Full production capacity at its Cilegon facility is currently 130,000 tonnes a year, but an upgrade is due to start this month and be completed in December. These works will boost the annual capacity to 160,000 tonnes for 2012, Iwasaki added.\par \par \uc2 Established in 1982, domestically focused Latinusa was once part of \uc2 PT Timah\uc2  but became a subsidiary of the world's No.4 steelmaker, \uc2 Nippon Steel\uc2  in late 2009.\par \par \uc2 Latinusa produces tinplate in coil and sheet forms, used for manufacturing mostly food and milk cans.\par \par \uc2 State-owned Timah, the world's largest integrated tin miner, supplies around 60 tonnes of tin ingot to Latinusa each month, using annual contracts tied to LME prices, Iwasaki said.\par \par \uc2 But since Oct. 1, Indonesian tin smelters have put in place a self-imposed export ban, with the aim of pushing prices above $25,000 a tonne.\par \par \uc2 "We're OK, no problem," he said about the impact of the ban, adding that the Indonesian smelter's export ban only affected international shipments. "We are just a domestic consumer."\par \par \uc2 Yet he said that tin prices are still high despite having lost about a third since hitting records in April and give Chinese tin makers an edge over the company.\par \par \uc2 "Our competitors are tinplate makers in China," Iwasaki said. "Judging the current situation, we cannot make money if tin prices are hiked."\par \par \uc2 London Metal Exchange tin hit a record high above $33,000 a tonne in April, but like other base metals, has since slumped as the global economic and demand outlook became increasingly uncertain. Tin traded at $22,600 at 0927 GMT.\par \par \uc2 "Current prices are still too high," said Iwasaki. "Three years ago, prices were about $15,000. Hot money has entered the tin market and so prices rise."\par \par \uc2 "In 2011, our major target is how to improve our competitiveness against China," he said, adding that prices below $20,000 a tonne best reflected the current supply and demand fundamentals.\par \par \uc2 "The Chinese (tinplate) prices never follow the trajection of raw material prices," he added. "China prices are almost dumping."\par \par \uc2 A crackdown on illegal mining, tighter export rules, falling onshore reserves and rain that had hindered production in Indonesia, which supplies about 30 percent of the world's tin consumption, helped drive the tin rally earlier this year.\par \par \uc2 FIRM PRICE OUTLOOK\par \par \uc2 The outlook for benchmark tin prices is looking increasingly supportive, however, as euro zone debt worries ease and top refined exporter Indonesia, implements an export ban.\par \par \uc2 World equities clambered out of bear market territory on Monday after a pledge from German and French leaders to come up with a plan by the end of the month to tackle Greece's confidence-sapping debt woes.\par \par \uc2 "Financial conditions in Europe are getting... better and better," said Iwasaki. "Hopefully, conditions will get better and better... in my opinion $18,000-$24,000 is a range for 2012."\par \par \uc2 Aside from a small trial of exports to India, which began three years ago, Latinusa's customers are mostly Indonesia-based, with almost 70 percent in greater Jakarta and 22 percent in Surabaya.\par \par \uc2 About 30 percent of the company's sales are in U.S. dollars and the rest in Indonesian rupiah, to try to minimise \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate fluctuations.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to stabilise the rupiah, causing the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves to fall.\par \par \uc2 "If they can keep the Indonesian rupiah against the U.S. dollar under 9,000, it is very good for us, especially for foreign investors to Indonesia," Iwasaki said.\par \par \uc2 ($1 = 8892.500 Indonesian Rupiahs)\par \par \uc2 (Editing by Ramthan Hussain)\par \par \uc2 INDONESIA-TIN/LATINUSA \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020111011e7ab000iv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
