\par\par \b \uc2 Indonesia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Reserves Fall To $114.5 Billion In Sept Vs $124.6 Billion In Aug\b0\par\par\uc2 293 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Oktober 2011\par 03:52\par \uc2 Dow Jones Business News\par \uc2 DJON\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 JAKARTA -(Dow Jones)- Indonesia's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves fell to $114.5 billion as of Sept. 30 from $124.6 billion a month earlier as the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to halt the rupiah's decline, data from Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  showed Friday.\par \par \uc2 Global investors have been trimming their holdings in riskier emerging markets assets due to combination of heightening risks of global economic slowdown and fears over euro zone debt, and like many other central banks in emerging Asia, Bank Indonesia has been spotted in the market trying to curb the volatility in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Many analysts, however, say that Indonesia is better positioned to withstand any potential turbulence in the financial markets thanks to its much-improved reserves and its vast domestic markets, which would shield the local economy should a global downturn occur.\par \par \uc2 The last time global risk aversion affected the country's financial assets was during the panic following the collapse of major investment bank \uc2 Lehman Brothers\uc2  in late 2008. Indonesia's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves stood at $50.6 Bln at the end of October 2008.\par \par \uc2 DBS said in a report this week that foreigners cut their holdings of rupiah-denominated government bonds by 12% in September from a month earlier, a pace similar to that seen in October 2008. However, this time around, the yield on 10-year government bonds only rose 12 basis points compared with a 410 basis points jump in October 2008 because local banks and Bank Indonesia were able to buy the bonds to help limit the price decline.\par \par \uc2 -By Andreas Ismar, Dow Jones Newswires, 62 21 39831277; andreasismar.sandiwan@dowjones.com [ 10-06-11 2152ET ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJON000020111007e7a70000b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
