\par\par \b \uc2 Dow Jones Asia-Pacific Top Stories Sked For October 7\b0\par\par\uc2 1,267 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Oktober 2011\par 09:05\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Following are the top Asia-Pacific stories featured on Dow Jones Newswires as of 0700 GMT. Not all stories appear on all wires. Please direct any questions or comments to asianewseds@dowjones.com.\par \par \uc2 MACRO/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /FIXED INCOME:\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: BOJ LEAVES POLICY ON HOLD, SAYS RECOVERY CONTINUING \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Japan on Friday kept its monetary policy on hold as widely expected, opting to stick with easing steps taken in August, as the strong yen and uncertainty over the global economy have yet to derail the nation's recovery. (published 0620 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: IMF SAYS RISKS TO AUSTRALIA OUTLOOK TILTED TO DOWNSIDE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Recent market volatility and a slowing in global growth means the risks to an otherwise robust outlook for Australia's economy are now tilted to the downside, the International Monetary Fund said Friday. (published 0454 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: BOK GOV: 2011 GDP GROWTH LIKELY LOWER THAN 4.3% FORECAST \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank of Korea Gov. Kim Choong-soo said Friday he expects the country's economic growth this year to come below the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's projection for a 4.3% rise, in his clearest indication yet that the BOK will cut its growth forecast for Asia's fourth-largest economy. (published 0410 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par S KOREA FINANCE MINISTER: SEE DOWNSIDE RISKS TO 2012 GROWTH FORECAST \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korean Finance Minister Bahk Jae-wan Friday acknowledged that there are downside risks to the government's forecast for 4.5% economic growth next year. (published 0301 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par DATA SNAP: INDIA PRIMARY ARTICLES WPI NEAR FLAT IN WEEK TO SEPT 24 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India's wholesale price index for primary articles was little changed at 202.4 in the week ended Sept. 24, compared with a provisional reading of 202.7 in the previous week, according to data issued Friday by the Ministry of Commerce and Industry. (published 0636 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par DATA SNAP: MALAYSIA AUGUST EXPORTS +10.9%; +9.4% EXPECTED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Malaysia's exports grew a stronger-than-expected 10.9% on-year in August, helped by a sharp increase in shipments of palm oil, chemicals and chemical products, liquefied natural gas and rubber products. (published 0401 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INDONESIA FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  RESERVES FALL ON \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves fell to $114.5 billion as of Sept. 30 from $124.6 billion a month earlier as the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to halt the rupiah's decline during the recent market selloff, data from Bank Indonesia showed Friday. (published 0701 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BANK INDONESIA DEPUTY GOV: EXPECT 'CONCRETE MEASURES' TO BOOST MARKET CONFIDENCE IN NEXT G-20 MEET \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank Indonesia expects "concrete measures" from a Group of 20 meeting of finance ministers and other officials from developed and developing economies next week, which will help boost market confidence, Deputy Gov. Hartadi Sarwono said Friday. (published 0528 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: THAI FINANCE MINISTER CRITICIZES MONETARY POLICY FOR SLOWING ECONOMY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Thai Finance Minister Thirachai Phuvanatnaranubala Friday criticized the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Thailand\f28 \uc2 \f2 's Monetary Policy Committee, saying it has put the brakes on the local economy too much and too soon. (published 0519 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par THAI \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : DOMESTIC DEMAND REMAINS SOLID DESPITE ONGOING FLOOD \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Thailand\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Friday that domestic demand remains solid despite severe flooding that has hit many parts of the country. (published 0632 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA'S ZHEJIANG PROVINCE TO ISSUE CNY8 BLN BONDS - REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The government of China's eastern Zhejiang province will issue CNY8 billion worth of bonds to fund infrastructure projects this year, as part of a trial that allows local governments to sell bonds directly, the state-run China Daily reported Thursday, without offering a timetable for the sale. (published 0250 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 EQUITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par 2ND UPDATE: \f28 \uc2 \f2 SAMSUNG ELECTRONICS\f28 \uc2 \f2  EXPECTS WEAK 3Q; TELECOM A BRIGHT SPOT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Samsung Electronics Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said it expects weaker third-quarter earnings, reflecting a decline in demand for its computer chips and flat panels, although brisk sales of its smartphones may help offset slower sales of other products. (published 0613 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: AUSTRALIAN JUDGEMENT ON APPLE, SAMSUNG CASE DELAYED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A judgment on whether to place a temporary ban on \f28 \uc2 \f2 Samsung Electronics Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . from selling a tablet device in Australia on the grounds that it copied \f28 \uc2 \f2 Apple Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 .'s has spilled into next week after a judge wasn't able to get her final ruling out by Friday. (published 0525 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BANDANNA CANCELS SALE PROCESS AFTER BIDS FALL SHORT-SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bandanna Energy Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . has failed to ride the wave of consolidation taking place in Australia's coal sector, closing its books to potential suitors after a sales process didn't generate adequate bids, a person familiar with the matter said. (published 0441 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par WOORI INVESTMENT & SECURITIES PLANS KRW600 BLN RIGHTS ISSUE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's Woori Investment & Securities Co. is planning to raise KRW600 billion via a rights offering to existing shareholders, the brokerage unit of Woori Finance Holdings Co. said Friday. (published 0554 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par SOFTBANK TO CHARGE LOWER IPHONE 4S MONTHLY FEE THAN \f28 \uc2 \f2 KDDI\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Softbank Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Friday that it will charge a fixed monthly data-communications fee of Y4,410 for the iPhone 4S, lower than rival \f28 \uc2 \f2 KDDI Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 .'s recently announced fee of Y4,980. (published 0406 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par TOYOTA PLANS TO START CAR EXPORTS FROM INDIA BY MARCH WITH ETIOS RANGE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Toyota Motor Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . plans to start exporting its cars from India by March as part of its strategy to make the South Asian country one of its key export hubs worldwide. (published 0441 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par QANTAS SAYS STRIKES TO HURT OVER 11,000 PASSENGERS MONDAY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Qantas Airways Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Friday that over 11,000 passengers will have their travel plans thrown into disarray Monday by strike action planned by engineers at Sydney, Melbourne and Brisbane airports. (published 0619 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par VIRGIN AUSTRALIA AUGUST PASSENGERS DOWN 2.7% ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Virgin Australia Ltd. Friday said it flew 2.7% less passengers in August compared with a year earlier, mostly due to a withdrawal from the domestic New Zealand market. (published 0146 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par SAN MIGUEL CONFIRMS TALKS WITH CIMB ON BANK OF COMMERCE UNIT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Philippine conglomerate \f28 \uc2 \f2 San Miguel Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . confirmed Friday it was in talks with \f28 \uc2 \f2 CIMB Group Holdings Bhd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . to sell a stake in its local banking arm, Bank of Commerce, to Malaysia's second largest bank by assets. (published 0232 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par SOME AIRBUS JETS MAY NEED WINDSHIELDS REPLACED - AUSTRALIAN GOVT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 European operators of Airbus A330s and A320s may be forced by regulators to replace aircraft windshields following cockpit fires on flights, the Australian government said Friday. (published 0446 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BECHTEL CORP\f28 \uc2 \f2  FORECASTS ONGOING INFRASTRUCTURE DEMAND \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The head of U.S. construction and engineering giant \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bechtel Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Friday he expected continuing global demand for infrastructure despite economic shocks to the world economy. (published 0558 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 TATA MOTORS\f28 \uc2 \f2  INTRODUCES PRIMA TRUCK, MANZA SEDAN IN SOUTH AFRICA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Tata Motors Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., India's largest auto maker by revenue, Friday introduced its Manza sedan and Prima range of trucks in South Africa at the Johannesburg International Motor Show. (published 0556 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ENERGY/COMMODITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: JAPAN EDANO TO VISIT UAE, SAUDI TO DISCUSS COOPERATION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's Minister of Economy, Trade and Industry Yukio Edano will visit the country's two largest suppliers of crude oil from Saturday to Tuesday to discuss economic and energy cooperation. (published 0517 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par INTERVIEW: QUEENSLAND MINERS MAY SEE A REPEAT OF LAST YEAR'S FLOODS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 While Australia's world class coal mining industry has yet to fully recover from the devastating floods in Queensland's Bowen Basin earlier this year, signs are emerging there is plenty to worry about in the approaching wet season. (published 0521 GMT) [ 07-10-11 0705GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 62550   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020111007e7a7000h6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
