\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Indonesia state insurers, banks told not to sell govt bonds\b0\par\par\uc2 532 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 September 2011\par 09:49\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds details, quotes)\par \par \uc2 JAKARTA, Sept 28 (Reuters) - Indonesia's government made a rare plea on Wednesday to state-owned insurance firms and banks not to sell government bonds as authorities try to stabilise volatile markets in the face of foreign selling over euro zone worries.\par \par \uc2 Authorities also urged large state firms to coordinate before they buy U.S. dollars, a step to protect Indonesia's struggling rupiah \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  which has fallen 4 percent against the dollar this month.\par \par \uc2 "State-owned insurance firms and banks have been urged not to sell government bonds when prices are volatile," Bambang Brodjonegoro, head of fiscal policy at the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , told reporters on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Three years after the collapse of Wall Street giant \uc2 Lehman Bros\uc2  sparked a stampede out of higher risk assets and sent emerging economies reliant on foreign funding into shock, such fears have resurfaced in recent days amid heavy emerging equity and bond losses accompanied by sharp \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakness.\par \par \uc2 The latest wave of foreign-led selling has been especially punishing on emerging-market darlings Indonesia, South Korea and Russia.\par \par \uc2 Foreign investors sold 14.05 trillion rupiah ($1.58 billion) of Indonesian government bonds from Sept. 16 to 26, reducing their ownership to 222.8 trillion rupiah, or 32 percent, of total outstanding bonds, the latest Finance Ministry data shows.\par \par \uc2 This compares to a record 251.23 trillion rupiah, or 35.7 percent, on Sept 9.\par \par \uc2 Indonesia's capital market regulator has also advised state-owned firms not to panic and sell stocks following volatility in Jakarta's benchmark stock index in recent days and heavy outflows of global capital.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  repeatedly in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to prop up the rupiah and buy government bonds in the secondary market. It had 124.64 trillion rupiah in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves as of the end of August.\par \par \uc2 Brodjonegoro also said the ministry had asked state firms to prepare funds to buy bonds if needed, under a scheme he called a bond stabilisation fund, to shore up the market.\par \par \uc2 But despite those headwinds, economists remain broadly upbeat about the outlook for Indonesia, Southeast Asia's biggest economy. The government expects economic growth of 6.5 percent this year, Foreign Minister Marty Natalegawa said on Tuesday, among the strongest in the region.\par \par \uc2 Brodjonegoro said the Finance Ministry now expects an inflation rate next year of 5 percent as the global economy slows. That compares with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's forecast for annual inflation of 4.8-4.9 percent for 2011.\par \par \uc2 Headline inflation rose to 4.79 percent in August from 4.61 percent in July, while core inflation jumped to 5.15 percent in August from July's 4.55 percent, data on Sept. 5 showed.\par \par \uc2 Perry Warjiyo, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's director of monetary policy and research, told reporters on Tuesday that Bank Indonesia may cut its benchmark reference rate to stimulate growth amid uncertainties in the global economy.\par \par \uc2 ($1 = 8,905 rupiah)\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Adriana Nina Kusuma and Fathiya Dahrul. Writing by Aditya Suharmoko. Editing by Jason Szep)\par \par \uc2 INDONESIA-ECONOMY/DEBT  (UPDATE 1)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110928e79s000be\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
