\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Indonesia's c.bank signals may cut rates\b0\par\par\uc2 366 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 September 2011\par 08:29\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  * C.bank repeats stands ready to cut rate to boost growth\par \par \uc2  * C.bank says sees inflation easing to below 5 percent this year\par \par \uc2  * C.bank says foreign reserves more than enough for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 (Adds details, qoutes)\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, Sept 27 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  signaled on Tuesday it may cut interest rates as Europe's debt crisis drives down the rupiah, stirs volatility in stock prices and takes a toll on Southeast Asia's biggest economy.\par \par \uc2  It was the second time in a month Bank Indonesia suggested it was willing to cut its benchmark reference rate to stimulate growth amid uncertainties in the global economy.\par \par \uc2  "Going forward, there is a room to lower the benchmark rate", the bank's director of monetary policy and research, Perry Warjiyo, told reporters. "Inflation pressure will continue to ease and this year it (CPI) will be below five percent."\par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  left its benchmark rate unchanged at 6.75 percent on Sept. 8 for a seventh straight month. But it  unexpectedly lowered the floor of its interbank overnight rates by half a percentage point to 150 basis points below the BI rate, which some analysts said was a form of policy easing.\par \par \uc2  Warjiyo also said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has more than enough foreign reserves to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  and stabilise the rupiah, which has shed as much as 5.9 percent this month. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Sept.22 for the first time bought government bonds in the secondary market and has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to prop up rupiah.\par \par \uc2  The Indonesian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit a seven-year high at the end of August, taking bond yields to record lows and stocks\par \par \uc2 to record highs. But as the outlook for global growth has soured, local policymakers have sounded increasingly nervous\par \par \uc2  about a reversal in sentiment. \par \par \uc2  The Jakarta Composite Index rebounded on Tuesday, rising 4 percent on the day, but it is down 10.5 percent this year after surging 46 percent last year, the biggest gain in Southeast Asia.   \par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Adriana Nina Kusuma. Writing by Janeman Latul. Editing by Jason Szep)\par \par \uc2 INDONESIA-ECONOMY/ (UPDATE 1)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110930e79r000cj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
