\par\par \b \uc2 DJ IMF Sees Slight Moderation In Asia Growth, Risks From EU, US\b0\par\par\uc2 353 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 September 2011\par 02:49\par \uc2 Dow Jones Chinese Financial Wire\par \uc2 DJCFWE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2011, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON (Dow Jones)--The International Monetary Fund said Saturday economic growth in Asia for this year and next will be slightly weaker from its April projection, with downside risks increasing as a result of the euro-zone debt crisis and the slowdown in the U.S.\par \par \uc2 "In line with the weaker global outlook, growth in Asia is expected to be slightly lower in 2011-2012 than we projected in April, but the expansion should remain healthy as the fundamentals for domestic demand remain strong," said Anoop Singh, director of the IMF's Asia Pacific department.\par \par \uc2 He said he now expects growth at between 7.5% and 8% in the next one to two years for developing Asia compared with an 8.4% projection in April.\par \par \uc2 Downside risks have increased from the global uncertainty and in particular an "escalation of the euro-area financial turbulence or a renewed slowdown in the United States could have substantial trade and financial spillovers to Asia."\par \par \uc2 "The turbulence in the markets this week underscores that Asia has not decoupled from advanced economies and remains greatly exposed to risks of contagion," he added.\par \par \uc2 Deputy IMF Director for Asia Mahmood Pradhan said he supports recent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, but he is skeptical of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the local bond market.\par \par \uc2 "Part of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  activity by Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  is to maintain liquidity. One-way flows make the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market very illiquid. So it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  not only to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  but also to maintain liquidity," he said.\par \par \uc2 Bank Indonesia said Thursday it sold dollars "in large amounts" to defend the rupiah and has also been buying rupiah-denominated government bonds to help stabilize the country's bond market from the turbulence in Europe and the U.S.\par \par \uc2 But Pradhan said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  should let yields rise and foreign investors should get used to it.\par \par \uc2 -By Costas Paris, Dow Jones Newswires; + 44 207842 9364; +44 7876577160; costas.paris@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 -0-\par \par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2011 \uc2 Dow Jones & Company, Inc\uc2 . \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJCFWE0020110926e79q000e2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
