\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Stock recovery,  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  help Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  trim losses\b0\par\par\uc2 1,279 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 August 2011\par 10:33\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * S.Korea authorities spotted selling dlr at around 1,096\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Taiwan c.banks also seen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * Talk of funds unwinding short euro/Asia positions\par \par \uc2 (Adds details, analyst comments)\par \par \uc2 By Jongwoo Cheon\par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, Aug 9 (Reuters) - Emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell on Tuesday on heavy stock outflows before \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and a recovery in the share markets helped them cut losses, but the near-term outlook remains cloudy on concerns about the Europe debt crises and U.S. economy.\par \par \uc2 Asian shares slumped in recent sessions, pulling down their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which had been benefiting from the region's growth story and the reluctance to hold euros due to the ongoing sovereign debt crisis in Europe.\par \par \uc2 "It looks difficult for sentiment on Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to revive anytime soon, although they may outperform others, as many investors have given up hopes for a sustained economic recovery," said Jeong My-young, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist of Samsung Futures in Seoul.\par \par \uc2 The extreme sell-off in risk assets has forced funds to square-up all risk positions and sell Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as well.\par \par \uc2 "Clearly, the risk factor dominates in the near-term, which pressures down Asian rates and \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2 . I have closed all my recommendations to pay Asian rates," said Frances Cheung, a strategist at \uc2 Credit Agricole\uc2  CIB in Hong Kong.\par \par \uc2 Shares recouped some of their losses, with traders citing speculation that the Fed might make an emergency statement before U.S. market opened as one of the reasons for the rebound, but most players were dismissive of the rumour.\par \par \uc2 To cushion the impact of a stock sell-off, some of the regional \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities, especially in Indonesia, South Korea and Taiwan, were spotted selling dollars to stem weakness in their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. The Taiwan dollar, helped by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , outperformed most of its Asian peers.\par \par \uc2 Policymakers are likely to keep providing relief to their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which are expected to stay weak as investors are likely to keep reducing risk exposure in a global rout, analysts and dealers said.\par \par \uc2 "We are on a slippery slope currently and any volatility that the authorities can control, they will try to," said Sacha Tihanyi, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist for Scotia Capital in Hong Kong.\par \par \uc2 "Given that high financial market volatility increases the negative downside risks to growth outlooks, and the softening in commodity prices, these central banks may be more amenable to entertaining \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakness. However, stemming volatility will also be a concern."\par \par \uc2 Investors are now focussing on the Federal Reserve's policy meeting later in the day amid mounting pressures on the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  for more actions to revive the economy and relive global markets.\par \par \uc2 The outlook remains dim.\par \par \uc2 "It (rebounds in stocks and Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) might be a bad development actually, with investors lured back to risk assets. But the risk is still to the downside if the ECB and Fed disappoint, for example," said \uc2 Credit Agricole\uc2  CIB's Cheung.\par \par \uc2 WON\par \par \uc2 The won recovered most of losses as the authorities were spotted selling dollars, especially around the dollar/won's session high of 1,096.1, to check the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's weakness.\par \par \uc2 Exporters also bought the South Korean \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for settlements.\par \par \uc2 The 14-day dollar/won Relative Strength Index (RSI) still stays above the 70 threshold, indicating the pair is in overbought territory, allowing the market to expect a rebound.\par \par \uc2 "We may see a sharp rise in the won after seeing such a severe fall. I don't think foreigners will sell stocks more," said a foreign bank dealer in Seoul.\par \par \uc2 Foreign investors sold a net 1.18 trillion won ($1.09 billion) in stocks, the largest since March 10 and outpacing their net purchases of bond futures of 998.8 billion won.\par \par \uc2 Bond inflows have also supported the won.\par \par \uc2 RUPIAH\par \par \uc2 The rupiah also cut losses as stock trimmed falls and after Indonesian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was spotted buying it for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Earlier, the Indonesian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  slid 0.6 percent to 8,555 per dollar, breaking through the 50 percent Fibonacci retracement of its appreciation since late June.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been actively supplying the dollar to maintain \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  volatility," says an Asian bank dealer in Jakarta, adding BI was seen at the moment.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been seen using a firm rupiah to fight inflation, but in a statement announcing its rate decision on Tuesday, Bank Indonesia said "it expects the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to remain stable with a tendency of limited appreciation."\par \par \uc2 Foreign investors sold a combined net $408.7 million in Indonesian stocks during the previous four consecutive sessions, according to Reuters data.\par \par \uc2 That compared with a 14-day moving average of net daily sales of $11.2 million.\par \par \uc2 PHILIPPINE PESO\par \par \uc2 The Philippine peso recovered most of earlier losses on caution over the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and regional stocks cut falls.\par \par \uc2 "Both local and foreign names buying this morning, but they are not too keen in pushing spot beyond 42.79," said a European bank dealer in Manila, referring dollar/peso's session high.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was expected to step in the market, if the peso weakens to 42.80, he added.\par \par \uc2 RINGGIT\par \par \uc2 The dollar is testing major resistance against the Malaysian ringgit at 3.0447. This is the 200-day moving average and has thwarted six attempts by the dollar to overcome it in the space of the last two years.\par \par \uc2 The dollar has not achieved a daily close above this index since 14 July 2009.\par \par \uc2 A daily close above this average is clearly bullish for the dollar and opens the possibility that its long term downtrend is coming to an end.\par \par \uc2 Investors still remain complacently long emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and may be forced to exit their positions as the global stock market rout takes its toll.\par \par \uc2 The dollar which currently trades at 3.0430 will face further major resistance at 3.0700.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par \par \uc