\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: USD/IDR Lower; 8,500-8,540 Band Tipped Wednesday\b0\par\par\uc2 156 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Juli 2011\par 11:30\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 0930 GMT [Dow Jones] The USD/IDR is lower at 8,510 from 8,525 in late Asian trade Monday on broad USD weakness against major regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Still, Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  was not seen to have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market, traders say, indicating the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is comfortable with the IDR's rise. "First, they want to curb inflation with a stronger \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Secondly, the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hasn't even gone near the psychological 8500 mark," says a local trader. Another trader says the prolonged U.S. debt ceiling impasse will weigh on the USD. He tips the USD/IDR to test the 8500 level near-term and expects a trading range of 8,500-8,540 Wednesday. (andreasismar.sandiwan@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in Singapore. 65 64154 140; MarketTalk@dowjones.com \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 [ 26-07-11 0930GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1012 1085 1848 5055 55109 75112   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110726e77q000ub\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
