\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Won, rupiah down on specs' dlr-short covering\b0\par\par\uc2 842 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Juli 2011\par 03:49\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Dlr short-covering, Lone Star rumour weigh on won\par \par \uc2 * Rupiah dips on corporate dlr demand\par \par \uc2 * Euro, weakening global economy may slow inflows to Asia\par \par \uc2 (Updates with text, prices)\par \par \uc2 By Jongwoo Cheon\par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, July 5 (Reuters) - The South Korean won and the Indonesian rupiah eased on Tuesday as interbank speculators covered dollar-short positions with the euro hit by a slew of stop-loss buying, but continuous inflows to Asia helped limit regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ' weakness.\par \par \uc2 "The uncertainty over the euro zone and the global economy may slow inflows to Asia, although flows could be quite volatile depending on sentiment," said Frances Cheung, a strategist at Credit Agricole CIB in Hong Kong.\par \par \uc2 "With the uncertainty, Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  can suffer from time to time in the near term."\par \par \uc2 Adding to the uncertainty over the outlook for the second half of the year for emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Australia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  trimmed its growth outlook for this year, while keeping interest rates on hold, as expected.\par \par \uc2 Emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  rose in the first half of the year, but their gains slowed in April-June on fears of a potential Greece debt default and signs of a slowing global economy.\par \par \uc2 But regional units have started the third quarter with a firm tone as foreign investors resumed buying stocks and bonds in the region, encouraged by stronger economic fundamentals than in many developed markets.\par \par \uc2 Long-term investors are unlikely stop injecting money into Asia as long as its robust growth is maintained, dealers and analysts said.\par \par \uc2 "The big picture won't be changed and USD/Asia still looks heavy," said a Kuala Lumpur-based dealer.\par \par \uc2 WON\par \par \uc2 The won retreated as investors covered dollar-short positions and on a market rumour about dollar demand linked to \uc2 Korea Exchange Bank\uc2 's dividend payment to Lone Star.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. buyout fund is set to secure a $466 million dividend payout from its stake in KEB.\par \par \uc2 Still, the South Korean \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  found relief from shipbuilders' demand for settlements and some investors such as offshore model funds bought it on dips.\par \par \uc2 "Offshore funds will absorb the won \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  assets whenever they have time and money. In longer term, the won's bullish trend remains intact," said a foreign bank dealer in Seoul.\par \par \uc2 Foreign investors bought Seoul stocks for five sessions in a row.\par \par \uc2 RUPIAH\par \par \uc2 The rupiah shed 0.2 percent to 8,540 versus the greenback on dollar-short covering and corporate demand.\par \par \uc2 Investors also remained cautious over possible dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with a dealer citing Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's aggressive dollar purchases around 8,518-8,525 in the previous session.\par \par \uc2 On Monday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's deputy governor said it sees the rupiah averaging 8,650 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 Still, the Indonesian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is seen staying firm despite caution over \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said a Japanese bank dealer in Jakarta, adding investors are likely to keep seeking higher yields.\par \par \uc2 "BI will guard it only when its moves are too volatile," the dealer said.\par \par \uc2 RINGGIT\par \par \uc2 The ringgit slightly fell against the dollar as interbank speculators covered dollar-short positions.\par \par \uc2 Still, rises in dollar/ringgit were capped ahead of some resistances such as 3.0135, around the bottom of the daily Ichimoku cloud.\par \par \uc2 Its 55-day moving average also stood at 3.0145.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par \par \uc2 Change on the day at 0710 GMT \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par Japan yen        81.14          80.77       -0.46\par Sing dlr        1.2275         1.2250       -0.20\par Taiwan dlr      28.778         28.752       -0.09\par Korean won     1066.20        1063.50       -0.25\par Baht             30.47          30.45       -0.07\par Peso             43.09          43.07       -0.05\par Rupiah         8540.00        8520.00       -0.23\par Rupee            44.49          44.43       -0.15\par Ringgit         3.0070         3.0030       -0.13\par Yuan            6.4669         6.4629       -0.06\par Change so far in 2011\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par Japan yen        81.14          81.15       +0.01\par Sing dlr        1.2275         1.2820       +4.44\par Taiwan dlr      28.778         30.368       +5.53\par Korean won     1066.20        1134.80       +6.43\par Baht             30.47          30.14       -1.08\par Peso             43.09          43.84       +1.75\par Rupiah         8540.00        9005.00       +5.44\par Rupee            44.49          44.70       +0.47\par Ringgit         3.0070         3.0820       +2.49\par Yuan            6.4669         6.5897       +1.90\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Additional reporting by Lee Soo-jung in SEOUL; Editing by Kim Coghill