\par\par \b \uc2 DJ UPDATE: Bank Indonesia Deputy Gov: Not Closed To Interest Rate-Hike Option\b0\par\par\uc2 664 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Juni 2011\par 07:59\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2011, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 --Indonesian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  isn't ruling out raising policy interest rate, even though inflation looks to be on downward trend, says deputy governor\par \par \uc2 --Room to manage inflation by letting rupiah appreciate isn't as big as before\par \par \uc2 --\b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , finance ministry in talks to use \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves to buy back government bonds.\par \par \uc2 (adds more comments from Hadad from 4th paragraph, remarks from finance minister in 14th-15th paragraphs) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By I Made Sentana and P.R. Venkat \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 JAKARTA (Dow Jones)--Bank Indonesia Deputy Governor Muliaman Hadad Sunday said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  isn't closed to the option of increasing interest rates, and cautioned that room to manage inflation by letting the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rise is not as "big" as before.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Indeed we see that inflation is on a downward trend for now. But I don't think we are closed to the option of hiking interest rates" Hadad told Dow Jones Newswires on the sidelines of the World Economic Forum on East Asia.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 He added that while the appreciation of the rupiah against the dollar helps to check imported inflation, "the room for maneuvering [inflation through \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  appreciation] is not so big as before."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hadad said that while domestic prices pressures need to be contained, a very strong local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  won't be good for the economy.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has said it will allow the rupiah to strengthen more against the U.S. dollar to help offset inflationary pressures. The rupiah has risen about 5.7% against the greenback so far this year, making it one the best performing among the major Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank Indonesia has held off on raising its policy interest rate even as inflation accelerated earlier this year, for fear of attracting speculative capital inflows. It has raised the rate just once since August 2009, and Thursday left the policy rate unchanged at 6.75%\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hadad also said that any increase in the reserve requirement ratio for commercial banks would depend on the amount of excess liquidity in the system.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has been using tools other than the policy rate to rein in inflation, including an increase of the mandatory reserve requirement ratio to 8% from 3% to tighten liquidity.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hadad also said the authorities were looking at ways to develop its bond markets to better manage the large capital flows entering \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 On \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to sterilize the excess liquidity, Hadad said that such moves are done in consultation with the finance ministry. "We do discuss this [\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ] very closely," he said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Speaking earlier at a WEF conference, Hadad said Bank Indonesia was optimistic on keeping inflation within target this year.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Indonesia's headline inflation is likely to be slightly more than 5% this year, within the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's target range of 4% to 6%, due to lower domestic food prices, an appreciating \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , and a lower chance of the government raising administered prices, Perry Warjiyo, a director at Bank Indonesia had said Friday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Indonesia's consumer price index rose nearly 7% through 2010.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 At the same conference, Indonesian Finance Minister Agus Martowardojo said that his country was not looking at implementing any capital controls and that his ministry was in talks with the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to use \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves to buy back government bonds.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 He said that the government and Bank Indonesia will sign an agreement that will allow the government to use the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves to stabilize the government's rupiah bond prices if investors dump the notes.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Foreigners currently hold around 30% of the government rupiah's bonds, one of the highest ratios in the region.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By I Made Sentana, and P.R. Venkat, Dow Jones Newswires, 62-39831277; i-made.sentana@dowjones.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 --Andreas Ismar and Linda Silaen contributed to this article.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 June 12, 2011 01:59 ET (05:59 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020110612e76c0003a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
