\par\par \b \uc2 DJ MARKET TALK: German Exporters More Bearish On EUR/CHF -Poll\b0\par\par\uc2 1,525 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 April 2011\par 11:34\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2011, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par Markettalk.eu@dowjones.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0934 GMT [Dow Jones] German export-orientated companies are more bearish on the medium-term outlook for EUR/CHF than a month ago, according to a poll conducted by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Commerzbank\f28 \uc2 \f2  in April. Of those questioned, 31% see six-month EUR/CHF appreciating, compared with 44% polled in March, the bank says. On the 12-month outlook, 33% expect EUR/CHF to gain, down from 46% of those polled a month ago, it adds. However in the short-term, three-month window, exporters are more bullish, with 37% predicting gains for EUR/CHF, compared with 32%, it notes. "Difficulties in the euro zone are likely to put pressure on the euro medium term, while the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Swiss National Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  will begin its rate rise cycle in summer." (neil.maclucas@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 0927 GMT [Dow Jones] The Sensex is off 0.3% at INR19,493.70, dragged by losses in \uc2 Reliance Industries\uc2  (500325.BY) on persistent concerns about falling output from the company's KG-D6 block, and after \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2  downgrades the stock to Neutral from Buy. "Reliance is weighing the market down, but there are no other negative triggers and the results today have been satisfactory," says a local analyst. He adds, markets are choppy ahead of the expiry of April derivatives Thursday. BSE market breadth is slightly negative with gainers lagging decliners 10 to 11. Reliance is down 1.4% at INR987.00. Wipro (507685.BY) is down 12.6% at INR451.95 after a lackluster earnings performance and a weak 1Q FY12 outlook. Among gainers: \uc2 Oil & Natural Gas Corp\uc2 . (500312.BY) is up 2.1% at INR310.00 and Maruti Suzuki (532500.BY) is 1.6% higher at INR1,321.75. ICICIdirect.com tips Sensex support at 19,300 and resistance at 19,630.(sudeep.jain@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0925 GMT [Dow Jones] The short sterling strip has moved sharply lower after the release of U.K. 1Q GDP data. The front 3 contracts have now reversed opening gains of up to 4bps and currently trade 2-4bps in negative territory. According to one dealer, the market is now pricing in 31bps of U.K. rate increases before year-end, before noting that overall this is not a "big move." (nick.cawley@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0922 GMT [Dow Jones] MPC meeting date SONIAs still price in the first U.K. rate hike in November after this morning's 1Q GDP reading, although expectations for a second hike have shifted forward to March, from April before the data. SONIA rates now price in an 80% probability of an October increase, from 67% before the release. (mark.brown@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0917 GMT [Dow Jones] Standard Chartered raises HK 2011 inflation forecast to 5.2% from 4.0% previously due to the still-rising food prices and faster-than-expected improvement in the labor market as the 1Q jobless rate of 3.4% was the lowest since mid-2008. "Food inflation should peak in 2H of 2011, but a tighter labor market would boost domestic demand and put upward pressure on prices," StanChart economist Kelvin Lau says, adding the private housing rents should keep rising for "a couple more quarters" which reflects the property boom of the past two years; rent rises usually lag property values because private housing tenants normally sign contracts that cover a year or more. The house keeps its 2012 inflation forecast of 4.0%. (chester.yung@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0912 GMT [Dow Jones] Malaysian shares end 0.2% higher at 1529.91 as market sentiment got a boost from gains in most regional markets. But the index was rangebound, with some investors staying away, awaiting the outcome of the FOMC meeting later in the global day, a local dealer says. Maybank IB says, "Range-trade the market with a very short-term time horizon. The index may still bounce around in a range-bound manner." It tips resistance at 1541, with support at 1525. Market breadth ends negative with 453 decliners vs 320 gainers. \uc2 Petronas Dagangan\uc2  (5681.KU) ends down 1.4% at MYR15.68, \uc2 Tenaga Nasional\uc2  (5347.KU) ends 0.7% down at MYR6.04. Among gainers, \uc2 MMC Corp\uc2 . (2194.KU) closes 1.5% higher at MYR2.66 and \uc2 Genting Bhd\uc2  (3182.KU) ends 1.4% higher at MYR11.66. (ankur.relia@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0911 GMT [Dow Jones] Indonesian shares end up 0.8% at a fresh record high of 3804.931 in moderate volume, led by foreign buying in most blue chips amid hopes for strong 1Q earnings and higher dividend payouts, traders say. They expect the market may continue to gain Thursday and tip the main index to top 3830. "The stronger rupiah and gains in most Asian markets helped improve overall sentiment here after recent sluggish performance," says a trader with Reliance Securities. Foreigners are net buyers of IDR337 billion worth of shares. Heavyweight Telkom (TLKM.JK) is up 3.4% at IDR7,700, \uc2 Bank Mandiri\uc2  (BMRI.JK) is up 2.1% at IDR7,150, while carmaker Astra (ASII.JK) is up 1.9% at IDR55,150 on bargain buying and hopes for higher dividend payouts. (edhi.pranasidhi@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0902 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/IDR is down at 8,625 from 8,645 late yesterday, but suspected Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  contains pair's slide, dealers say. Three dealers suspected the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to have bought around $50 million at 8,625 to prevent the pair from falling too fast. "I still think Bank Indonesia will tolerate a further fall in the dollar to help curb imported inflation," one of traders says; he expects the USD will be supported around 8,600 for now as it's already oversold, and tips a 8,610-8,640 range for Thursday. (i-made.sentana@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0856 GMT [Dow Jones] Westpac Institutional Bank recommends selling the USD/IDR, noting that despite recent gains "we still see scope for Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to play catch up." In a note to clients, the house recommends selling the USD/IDR in the 1-month NDF around the 8640 level, with an initial target of 8500, and stop-loss orders just above 8850. The house adds that despite gains against the USD, many Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  including the KRW and the IDR are still lagging in terms of nominal effective exchange rate. The IDR in particular is a good bet because "the fundamentals of the economy are sound and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is happy to let the exchange rate strengthen to help curb inflation pressures," \uc2 Westpac\uc2  says. (martin.vaughan@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0849 GMT [Dow Jones] June gilt contract falls by 12-14 ticks immediately after announcement of U.K. preliminary numbers for 1Q GDP, showing in-line growth of 0.5%. Short sterling market has reversed earlier gains and currently trades flat to 2 ticks lower on day after traders had built up expectations that GDP reading would be worse than forecast. June contract currently 23 ticks lower on session at 118.84; 2-year cash yields 1.114%, up 3bps; 10-year cash yields 3.514%, also up 3bps. (nick.cawley@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0842 GMT [Dow Jones] India short-end overnight indexed swaps are near steady in the absence of any triggers during the session as traders stay cautious ahead of the RBI's rate-setting meeting on May 3, a dealer at a privately-run bank says. The one-year OIS is at 7.80%/7.84% from 7.81%/7.84% late Tuesday and the five-year OIS is at 8.27%/8.31% from 8.28%/8.31%. "Most in the swap market have built positions for a 50 bp hike and are now cautious before the policy meet. If the weekly food and fuel inflation data tomorrow throws some surprises, you may see some major swings," the dealer says. He adds, the long-end is also ranged tracking similar movement in bond yields. He tips the one-year OIS in a 7.78%-7.85% band for the session.(sourav.mishra@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0838 GMT [Dow Jones] The USD/PHP is a tad lower, in-line with regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ' advance against the USD, and on better-than-expected fiscal performance in March. However, the pair's decline was tempered by suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , say two traders. The pair is at 43.21 from 43.28 late Tuesday. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have bought around $80 million between 43.17-43.20, says one trader, who adds that the pair is likely to be rangebound Thursday in a 43.00-43.35 band. "Because of expectations of (\b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  near the 43.00 level, people are wary to add to their short USD positions," the trader says. The market will also closely monitor the outcome of the FOMC meeting later in the global day, traders add. (rhea.sandique-carlos@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 April 27, 2011 05:34 ET (09:34 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020110427e74r00273\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
