\par\par \b \uc2 DJ Emerging Nations Seen Taking More Subdued Tone On  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  Wars\b0\par\par\uc2 919 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 April 2011\par 04:48\par \uc2 Dow Jones Chinese Financial Wire\par \uc2 DJCFWE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2011, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 --Emerging nations may be less strident on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciation at coming IMF/World Bank meetings\par \par \uc2 --Inflation makes emerging countries more open to \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciation\par \par \uc2 --Capital controls, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  battles to remain an issue By Anjali Cordeiro Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES\par \par \uc2 NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--After a year of aggressive moves to beat down their exchange rates, emerging nations are quietly showing a greater acceptance for stronger \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as they battle rising inflation at home.\par \par \uc2 Some of that willingness to allow \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciation may be reflected in the tone of finance ministers and central bankers from the developing world as they gather for the 2011 Spring meetings of the World Bank and International Monetary Fund in Washington later this week.\par \par \uc2 As with previous such meetings, there is still likely to be finger pointing. Developing nations continue to blame loose monetary policy in the U.S. as a cause of potential asset bubbles and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciation in Asia and Latin America. They also face pressure from their exporters to keep \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  weak due to competition from China, which tightly controls the yuan. But those worries are temporarily taking a back seat to local price pressures.\par \par \uc2 'I wouldn't expect the same stridency around \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  that we have seen in some recent meetings, nor will the issue disappear,' says Mark Malloch-Brown, a former vice president of the World Bank, who is now at FTI Consulting.\par \par \uc2 For investors, the growing possibility that policymakers will be more flexible makes Latin American and Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  an attractive proposition. The dollar has lost 5.6% against the real and 1.4% against the Indonesia rupiah since mid March. A stronger \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which reduces the price of imports, can help reduce inflation.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's Finance Minister Guido Mantega, who used the term '\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  wars' to describe global disagreements on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 , last year raised taxes on foreign fixed-income investments into the country. But as the real soared over the last month, investors grew hopeful that Brazilian policymakers will take a softer stance.\par \par \uc2 While Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has continued to build reserves, there have been no stringent capital controls announced. Policymakers there are battling inflation, with data showing a rise in the 12-month inflation rate to 6.3% as of March.\par \par \uc2 Bank Indonesia's deputy governor said recently that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will continue to fight inflation and prevent the rupiah from being overly volatile. Those comments could suggest the bank might be open to allowing the rupiah to rise somewhat to fight inflation, but it would want any moves to be smooth.\par \par \uc2 'Indonesia changed their tune,' said David Rolley, portfolio manager at Loomis, Sayles & Co. 'All these central banks had to decide what war to fight. They are now much more interested in fighting inflation than a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  war.'\par \par \uc2 One issue likely to be hotly debated at the meetings is the efficacy of capital controls and government \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . In a reversal of its earlier stance, the International Monetary Fund recently endorsed the use of controls on international cash inflows in certain cases.\par \par \uc2 But it is still unclear how effective such policy tools have been in curbing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  increases in places like Brazil and South Korea. These \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have risen even though policymakers have taken steps to curb so-called 'hot money' flows.\par \par \uc2 Emerging nations are unlikely to completely throw in the towel. Central banks in South Korea, Malaysia and \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  appeared to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in recent weeks as their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  jumped, though their main focus appears to be to stem appreciation rather than reverse the direction of their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Emerging Asian countries, excluding China, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in spot \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets by an estimated $11 billion in March and $15.3 billion in February, according to \uc2 Barclays Capital\uc2 . This compares to an average of $22.6 billion per month between August and October last year, when such \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  were more aggressive.\par \par \uc2 Emerging-market policymakers generally compare their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  versus others in the developing world. So, they tend to be more comfortable if all emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are appreciating at the same time, says Denise Simon, a portfolio manager on the Lazard emerging-markets debt team in New York.\par \par \uc2 'I don't know if individually countries can do anything' to reverse the upward trend in their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said Simon, whose team likes Asian and Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  because of the fundamental strength of these economies and widening interest rate differentials.\par \par \uc2 Emerging world central banks have begun raising interest rates, even as rates in the U.S. and Japan remain near zero. The International Monetary Fund in its World Economic Outlook noted that some emerging economies will need even tighter monetary policies to reduce the risk of a hard landing. In most of these economies, some appreciation of the exchange rate is called for, the IMF said.\par \par \uc2 Philip Poole, head of macro and investments strategy at \uc2 HSBC Global Asset Management\uc2 , says China's recent moves to let the yuan to move a little higher makes it easier for other emerging nations to allow appreciation. \b \highlight22\uc2 Currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  like the Singapore dollar and Korean won look attractive, he feels, and even the Brazilian real could rise some more.\par \par \uc2 But he doesn't expect any broad consensus or coordination on emerging \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the IMF meetings: 'It's each man for himself.' -By Anjali Cordeiro; Dow Jones Newswires; 212-416-2200; anjali.cordeiro@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 -0-\par \par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2011 \uc2 Dow Jones & Company, Inc\uc2 . \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJCFWE0020110413e74d0025u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
