\par\par \b \uc2 DJ MARKET TALK: India Call Rate Likely Below 6% N/T On RBI Measures\b0\par\par\uc2 1,781 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 April 2011\par 07:29\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2011, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in Singapore. 65 64154 140; MarketTalk@dowjones.com \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 0529 GMT [Dow Jones] India's overnight call rate is likely to remain below 6.0% for the next two weeks on a positive banking system cash situation and as the RBI extends the second liquidity facility until March 6, says a dealer with a privately-run bank. The measures were set to expire Friday. The RBI says banks can avail liquidity up to 1.0% of their net deposits and can apply for a waiver if they fall short of the mandated bond-holding ratio due to this measure. "This will flush the banking system with liquidity in the short-term but may not be sustainable in the long-run," the dealer adds. The interbank overnight call rate is at 5.85% unchanged from Thursday's close, while the three-day call rate is at 6.0%. The collateralized borrowing and lending obligation rate or CBLO is at 2.16% from 3.25% at the open. The dealer tips the overnight call rate in a 5.00%-6.00% range in the near-term.(sourav.mishra@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0523 GMT [Dow Jones] S&P's upgrade of Indonesia sovereign ratings raises expectations the country could get the long-coveted investment grade by the three major ratings agency by 2012, says Standard Chartered economist Eric Sugandi. "One of them could upgrade in 2011," he says. S&P raised its long-term foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  sovereign credit and debt ratings to BB+ with a positive outlook from BB. Its ratings are now at par with Fitch's BB+ (positive), and \uc2 Moody's\uc2  Ba1 (stable outlook). Analysts don't expect S&P's action to push bond prices much higher after their recent rally. "Bond yields have been very low," Danamon bond analyst Helmi Arman says. (i-made.sentana@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0520 GMT (Dow Jones) The near-term risk for USD/CHF has reverted to the downside, and a retracement into the 0.9025 area is possible, says \uc2 Commerzbank\uc2 . "Intraday rallies are likely to find near term resistance at 0.9225 ahead of 0.9300," according to analyst Karen Anne Jones. The USD/CHF is at 0.9101 by 0515 GMT. (neil.maclucas@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0512 GMT [Dow Jones] An investor sells with-delta one-month USD-call/JPY-put contract with a Y86.00 strike at 10.65% earlier in the day, while some other players sell three-month at-the-money straddles, says a senior dealer at a major Japanese bank. Traded contracts suggest "investors believe the USD/JPY will eventually rise above Y86.00, but not at a speed that the current volatilities suggest now," he says, adding that current USD/JPY volatilities are bit overpriced due to the Japan-quake risk premium. Benchmark volatilities implied by one-month ATM volatilities rise to 10.05%/10.75% from 10.25%/10.55% in New York; the dealer says ongoing concerns about Fukushima nuclear reactors are a part of the reason.(takashi.mochizuki@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0507 GMT [Dow Jones] Singapore STI is up marginally, gaining 2.89 points, or 0.1%, to 3174.54 at lunch after opening weaker as markets in Japan recover smartly from a lackluster start after Thursday's earthquake. "We may see some profit-taking again moving into the weekend. The markets are likely to remain cautious. A lot will depend on how the European markets react to the ECB rate hike," says OCBC analyst Carey Wong. Support for the benchmark is tipped below 3165 and then 3130 and resistance at 3180 followed by 3200. SGX (S68.SG) is among the top gainers, +2.7% at S$8.37 as Australia formally rejects merger plans with ASX (ASX.AU). \uc2 Sembcorp Industries\uc2  (U96.SG) is the top gainer, up 3.0% at S$5.51 and its rig building unit \uc2 Sembcorp Marine\uc2  (S51.SG) is up 1.2% at S$6.00 on a spurt in crude oil prices. \uc2 Keppel Corp\uc2 . (BN4.SG) is up 0.2% at S$12.70. (gaurav.raghuvanshi@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0505 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/IDR slides further to 8,653 vs 8,660 earlier in the day and 8,672 late yesterday as news of Indonesia's long-term foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  sovereign credit and debt ratings upgrade by S&P to BB+ from BB fuels more inflows, dealers say. "Although S&P was behind other ratings agencies its ratings action on Indonesia, it's still good news for Indonesia as now all three major ratings agencies have acknowledged Indonesia's progress," a dealer says; three dealers suspect Bank Indonesia to have bought around $100 million at the 8,653 level to ease volatility. "Despite Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the market still looks intent to drive the dollar lower," one of the dealers say. A 8,645-8,660 range is tipped. (i-made.sentana@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0504 GMT [Dow Jones] The Nikkei is up 1.5% at 9733.80, well up from its midday close of 9678.68, as limited damage from Thursday night's powerful earthquake, combined with a robust forecast from heavyweight \uc2 Fast Retailing\uc2  (9983.TO) continue to lift the index, says Hideyuki Ishiguro, a strategist at \uc2 Okasan Securities\uc2 . "The absence of further bad news on the nuclear crisis and (\uc2 Fast Retailing\uc2  unit) Uniqlo's rosy forecast are boosting the mood of the market," he says, adding that there's also been some short-covering ahead of the weekend. 30/33 Topix subindexes are now higher, with retailers, securities and insurance stocks outperforming. \uc2 Fast Retailing\uc2  is up 6.9% at Y11,900. \uc2 Tokyo Electric Power\uc2  (9501.TO) is up 14% at Y388, due mostly to short-covering. Exporters are generally benefiting from a more favorable USD/JPY (now 85.03); Advantest (6857.TO) is up 3.1% at Y1,539. Nintendo (7974.OK) is off 2.4% at Y20,520 after a target price cut by \uc2 Barclays Capital\uc2 . (judy.lam@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0501 GMT [Dow Jones] The USD/SGD is at 1.2570 vs 1.2609 early trade after hitting a fresh record low of 1.2564 in line with gains in most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and an increase in risk appetite, says trader with a foreign bank. "There are fund inflows happening and expectations here are building that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will tighten (\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) policy at its meeting next week," says a trader with a foreign bank; he adds that it is difficult to provide a support level given that the pair is now moving into unchartered territory. (venkat.pr@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0457 GMT [Dow Jones] Vietnam shares end up 0.2% at 464.29 with some long-term investors buying blue chips, analysts say. "Big investors, especially investment funds, are quietly buying shares of companies with large market capitalization," says Quach Manh Hao, Deputy Director of Thang Long Securities. "They are confident the index will rise above 500 towards the year-end, with the recovery of the economy," he adds. "Short-term players are still leaving their money idle, waiting for more 1Q audited earning results due from the middle of this month," he says. Volume is thin with 20.3 million shares valued at VND464.67 billion. Among the most active shares, \uc2 Vietnam Mechanization Electrification & Construction JSC\uc2  (MCG.VH) ends up 4.2% at VND15,000, \uc2 Saigon Thuong Tin Commercial Joint Stock Bank\uc2  (STB.VH), or \uc2 Sacombank\uc2 , is down 1.4% at VND13,800 and stock broker \uc2 Saigon Securities Inc\uc2 . (SSI.VH) closes 1.3% lower at VND22,000. (trong-khanh.vu@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0455 GMT [Dow Jones] Indonesian shares are up 0.3% at 3740.191 in light volume midday, led by gains in banks, consumer-and commodity-related stocks amid hopes for strong 1Q earnings, traders say. They expect news that S&P raises Indonesia Foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Ratings To BB+ From BB to inspire further buying in the afternoon session, and tip the main index to test the 3750 resistance level. "(The S&P news) came near the lunch break so that is why it's hasn't much affected sentiment here," says a trader with Valbury Securities. The upgrade will make the IDR a more attractive investment; with more investors buying, a stronger IDR is good for companies as it may lower their debt burden and reduce the cost of imported raw materials, which should inspire buying in stocks. Foreigners are net buyers of IDR120 billion worth of shares. Among gainers are Bank Rakyat (BBRI.JK), up 1.6% at IDR6,300, tin producer Timah (TINS.JK), up 3.7% at IDR2,900, and consumer goods producer Mayora (MYOR.JK) rising 3.2% to IDR11,50. (edhi.pranasidhi@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0447 GMT [Dow Jones] Philippine shares extend gains, ending at a fresh 5-month high, buoyed by expectations of good corporate earning results in 1Q, say traders. The benchmark PSEi is up 0.5% at 4241, gaining 21 points amid heavy trading. Grace Cerdenia, \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  head at 2TradeAsia.com, says the stock market is also attracting investors looking for higher yields given the overall liquidity in the local financial system. Cerdenia thinks the market may consolidate next week with the index likely to stay within a 4180-4250 band. Most active stocks include PLDT (TEL.PH) which is off 0.2% at PHP2,346, Alliance Global (AGI.PH) up 0.9% at PHP11.30, and \uc2 Aboitiz Power\uc2  (AP.PH) up 1.3% at PHP32.10. (rhea.sandique-carlos@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0445 GMT [Dow Jones] The KLCI is a tad lower, down 0.24 point at 1561.69 at midday. "The index is still in a consolidation phase, especially since there are no particular leads to trade on," a local trader says. He adds, investors tend to remain cautious ahead of the weekend. He tips a tight 1555-1565 range for the rest of the day. Market breadth is slightly negative with 351 losers compared with 332 gainers. Tenaga (5347.KU) is down 1.0% at MYR6.13, \uc2 IOI Corp\uc2 . (1961.KU) is down 0.9% at MYR5.67 and Gamuda (5398.KU) is down 0.8% at MYR3.89. Among gainers, \uc2 Hong Leong Bank\uc2  (5819.KU) is up 2.7% at MYR10.68, \uc2 Hong Leong Financial Group\uc2  (1082.KU) is up 1.3% at MYR9.49 and \uc2 Genting Bhd\uc2 . (3182.KU) is up 1.1% at MYR11.36. (ankur.relia@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 April 08, 2011 01:29 ET (05:29 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020110408e748000wn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
