ise to 10.05%/10.75% from 10.25%/10.55% in New York; the dealer says ongoing concerns about Fukushima nuclear reactors are a part of the reason.(takashi.mochizuki@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0507 GMT [Dow Jones] Singapore STI is up marginally, gaining 2.89 points, or 0.1%, to 3174.54 at lunch after opening weaker as markets in Japan recover smartly from a lackluster start after Thursday's earthquake. "We may see some profit-taking again moving into the weekend. The markets are likely to remain cautious. A lot will depend on how the European markets react to the ECB rate hike," says OCBC analyst Carey Wong. Support for the benchmark is tipped below 3165 and then 3130 and resistance at 3180 followed by 3200. SGX (S68.SG) is among the top gainers, +2.7% at S$8.37 as Australia formally rejects merger plans with ASX (ASX.AU). \uc2 Sembcorp Industries\uc2  (U96.SG) is the top gainer, up 3.0% at S$5.51 and its rig building unit \uc2 Sembcorp Marine\uc2  (S51.SG) is up 1.2% at S$6.00 on a spurt in crude oil prices. \uc2 Keppel Corp\uc2 . (BN4.SG) is up 0.2% at S$12.70. (gaurav.raghuvanshi@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0505 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/IDR slides further to 8,653 vs 8,660 earlier in the day and 8,672 late yesterday as news of Indonesia's long-term foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  sovereign credit and debt ratings upgrade by S&P to BB+ from BB fuels more inflows, dealers say. "Although S&P was behind other ratings agencies its ratings action on Indonesia, it's still good news for Indonesia as now all three major ratings agencies have acknowledged Indonesia's progress," a dealer says; three dealers suspect Bank Indonesia to have bought around $100 million at the 8,653 level to ease volatility. "Despite Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the market still looks intent to drive the dollar lower," one of the dealers say. A 8,645-8,660 range is tipped. (i-made.sentana@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0504 GMT [Dow Jones] The Nikkei is up 1.5% at 9733.80, well up from its midday close of 9678.68, as limited damage from Thursday night's powerful earthquake, combined with a robust forecast from heavyweight \uc2 Fast Retailing\uc2  (9983.TO) continue to lift the index, says Hideyuki Ishiguro, a strategist at \uc2 Okasan Securities\uc2 . "The absence of further bad news on the nuclear crisis and (\uc2 Fast Retailing\uc2  unit) Uniqlo's rosy forecast are boosting the mood of the market," he says, adding that there's also been some short-covering ahead of the weekend. 30/33 Topix subindexes are now higher, with retailers, securities and insurance stocks outperforming. \uc2 Fast Retailing\uc2  is up 6.9% at Y11,900. \uc2 Tokyo Electric Power\uc2  (9501.TO) is up 14% at Y388, due mostly to short-covering. Exporters are generally benefiting from a more favorable USD/JPY (now 85.03); Advantest (6857.TO) is up 3.1% at Y1,539. Nintendo (7974.OK) is off 2.4% at Y20,520 after a target price cut by \uc2 Barclays Capital\uc2 . (judy.lam@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0501 GMT [Dow Jones] The USD/SGD is at 1.2570 vs 1.2609 early trade after hitting a fresh record low of 1.2564 in line with gains in most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and an increase in risk appetite, says trader with a foreign bank. "There are fund inflows happening and expectations here are building that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will tighten (\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) policy at its meeting next week," says a trader with a foreign bank; he adds that it is difficult to provide a support level given that the pair is now moving into unchartered territory. (venkat.pr@dowjones.com) [ 04-08-11 0139ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022  \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020110408e7480003o\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
