\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: USD/THB Lower; 30.00 Support Tipped - Dealers\b0\par\par\uc2 1,745 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 April 2011\par 07:31\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in Singapore. 65 64154 140; MarketTalk@dowjones.com \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0531 GMT [Dow Jones] The USD/THB slips to 30.03-30.04 from 30.06-30.07 early, and compared with 30.11-30.115 late Thursday in active trade, in line with most regional peers, say traders. The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Thailand\f28 \uc2 \f2  is suspected to have bought the dollar since early trade, say two local dealers; they expect the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to be around for the entire day to slow the baht's rise. One local dealer adds that continued capital inflows, in addition to exporters' selling, are pushing the greenback lower. Another dealer says the rising interest rate trend amid robust economic growth in Asia is likely to continue to attract more fund inflows. Dealers tip support at 30.00 for today. (piyarat.setthasiriphaiboon@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 0529 GMT [Dow Jones] India's overnight call rate is likely to remain below 6.0% for the next two weeks on a positive banking system cash situation and as the RBI extends the second liquidity facility until March 6, says a dealer with a privately-run bank. The measures were set to expire Friday. The RBI says banks can avail liquidity up to 1.0% of their net deposits and can apply for a waiver if they fall short of the mandated bond-holding ratio due to this measure. "This will flush the banking system with liquidity in the short-term but may not be sustainable in the long-run," the dealer adds. The interbank overnight call rate is at 5.85% unchanged from Thursday's close, while the three-day call rate is at 6.0%. The collateralized borrowing and lending obligation rate or CBLO is at 2.16% from 3.25% at the open. The dealer tips the overnight call rate in a 5.00%-6.00% range in the near-term.(sourav.mishra@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0523 GMT [Dow Jones] S&P's upgrade of Indonesia sovereign ratings raises expectations the country could get the long-coveted investment grade by the three major ratings agency by 2012, says Standard Chartered economist Eric Sugandi. "One of them could upgrade in 2011," he says. S&P raised its long-term foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  sovereign credit and debt ratings to BB+ with a positive outlook from BB. Its ratings are now at par with Fitch's BB+ (positive), and \uc2 Moody's\uc2  Ba1 (stable outlook). Analysts don't expect S&P's action to push bond prices much higher after their recent rally. "Bond yields have been very low," Danamon bond analyst Helmi Arman says. (i-made.sentana@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0520 GMT (Dow Jones) The near-term risk for USD/CHF has reverted to the downside, and a retracement into the 0.9025 area is possible, says \uc2 Commerzbank\uc2 . "Intraday rallies are likely to find near term resistance at 0.9225 ahead of 0.9300," according to analyst Karen Anne Jones. The USD/CHF is at 0.9101 by 0515 GMT. (neil.maclucas@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0512 GMT [Dow Jones] An investor sells with-delta one-month USD-call/JPY-put contract with a Y86.00 strike at 10.65% earlier in the day, while some other players sell three-month at-the-money straddles, says a senior dealer at a major Japanese bank. Traded contracts suggest "investors believe the USD/JPY will eventually rise above Y86.00, but not at a speed that the current volatilities suggest now," he says, adding that current USD/JPY volatilities are bit overpriced due to the Japan-quake risk premium. Benchmark volatilities implied by one-month ATM volatilities rise to 10.05%/10.75% from 10.25%/10.55% in New York; the dealer says ongoing concerns about Fukushima nuclear reactors are a part of the reason.(takashi.mochizuki@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0507 GMT [Dow Jones] Singapore STI is up marginally, gaining 2.89 points, or 0.1%, to 3174.54 at lunch after opening weaker as markets in Japan recover smartly from a lackluster start after Thursday's earthquake. "We may see some profit-taking again moving into the weekend. The markets are likely to remain cautious. A lot will depend on how the European markets react to the ECB rate hike," says OCBC analyst Carey Wong. Support for the benchmark is tipped below 3165 and then 3130 and resistance at 3180 followed by 3200. SGX (S68.SG) is among the top gainers, +2.7% at S$8.37 as Australia formally rejects merger plans with ASX (ASX.AU). \uc2 Sembcorp Industries\uc2  (U96.SG) is the top gainer, up 3.0% at S$5.51 and its rig building unit \uc2 Sembcorp Marine\uc2  (S51.SG) is up 1.2% at S$6.00 on a spurt in crude oil prices. \uc2 Keppel Corp\uc2 . (BN4.SG) is up 0.2% at S$12.70. (gaurav.raghuvanshi@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0505 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/IDR slides further to 8,653 vs 8,660 earlier in the day and 8,672 late yesterday as news of Indonesia's long-term foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  sovereign credit and debt ratings upgrade by S&P to BB+ from BB fuels more inflows, dealers say. "Although S&P was behind other ratings agencies its ratings action on Indonesia, it's still good news for Indonesia as now all three major ratings agencies have acknowledged Indonesia's progress," a dealer says; three dealers suspect Bank Indonesia to have bought around $100 million at the 8,653 level to ease volatility. "Despite Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the market still looks intent to drive the dollar lower," one of the dealers say. A 8,645-8,660 range is tipped. (i-made.sentana@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0504 GMT [Dow Jones] The Nikkei is up 1.5% at 9733.80, well up from its midday close of 9678.68, as limited damage from Thursday night's powerful earthquake, combined with a robust forecast from heavyweight \uc2 Fast Retailing\uc2  (9983.TO) continue to lift the index, says Hideyuki Ishiguro, a strategist at \uc2 Okasan Securities\uc2 . "The absence of further bad news on the nuclear crisis and (\uc2 Fast Retailing\uc2  unit) Uniqlo's rosy forecast are boosting the mood of the market," he says, adding that there's also been some short-covering ahead of the weekend. 30/33 Topix subindexes are now higher, with retailers, securities and insurance stocks outperforming. \uc2 Fast Retailing\uc2  is up 6.9% at Y11,900. \uc2 Tokyo Electric Power\uc2  (9501.TO) is up 14% at Y388, due mostly to short-covering. Exporters are generally benefiting from a more favorable USD/JPY (now 85.03); Advantest (6857.TO) is up 3.1% at Y1,539. Nintendo (7974.OK) is off 2.4% at Y20,520 after a target price cut by \uc2 Barclays Capital\uc2 . (judy.lam@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0501 GMT [Dow Jones] The USD/SGD is at 1.2570 vs 1.2609 early trade after hitting a fresh record low of 1.2564 in line with gains in most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and an increase in risk appetite, says trader with a foreign bank. "There are fund inflows happening and expectations here are building that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will tighten (\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) policy at its meeting next week," says a trader with a foreign bank; he adds that it is difficult to provide a support level given that the pair is now moving into unchartered territory. (venkat.pr@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0457 GMT [Dow Jones] Vietnam shares end up 0.2% at 464.29 with some long-term investors buying blue chips, analysts say. "Big investors, especially investment funds, are quietly buying shares of companies with large market capitalization," says Quach Manh Hao, Deputy Director of Thang Long Securities. "They are confident the index will rise above 500 towards the year-end