aysian shares end 0.2% lower at 1553.07 as investors book profits after recent gains, a local dealer says. OSK Research says, "it is likely that the index will start to consolidate before resuming its mission to re-test the historic peak at 1577 points." It tips immediate support at 1547 followed by another strong support at the 1531-1536 level. The dealer adds that construction stocks continue to attract demand as investors expect more new projects to be awarded by the government in coming days. The construction sub-index ends up 0.7%. Market breadth is negative with 492 losers compared with 348 gainers. Genting Malaysia (4715.KU) ends down 3.2% at MYR3.68, RHB Capital (1066.KU) closes 1.4% lower at MYR8.58 and Axiata (6888.KU) ends down 0.8% at MYR4.82. Among gainers, \uc2 Berjaya Food Bhd\uc2  (5196.KU) closes up 38% at MYR1.14, \uc2 Multi-Purpose Holdings\uc2  (3859.KU) ends up 3.4% at MYR2.76 and \uc2 Malaysian Airline System\uc2  (3786.KU) closes up 1.6% at MYR1.86. (ankur.relia@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0851 GMT [Dow Jones] The USD/PHP is a tad higher late as some banks cover short-USD positions as the EUR weakened following \uc2 Moody's\uc2  downgrade of Portugal's long-term government bond rating, say traders. The pair is at 43.35 from 43.31 late Monday amid heavy trading. A local dealer says the USD/PHP may continue to move higher Wednesday as the market focuses on how the EUR will react during U.S. trade to Portugal's bond rating downgrade; next resistance is tipped at 43.50 with support at 43.35. (rhea.sandique-carlos@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0850 GMT [Dow Jones] Treasurys are treading water in London, with trading confined to narrow ranges. The ISM non-manufacturing report is out at 1400 GMT while minutes of the previous meeting of the FOMC are published at 1800 GMT. Speakers include Minneapolis Fed's Kocherlakota and Treasury Secretary Geithner. The 2-year note is unchanged at 99-31+/32 to yield 0.752%. The 10-year note is steady at 101-23+/32, yielding 3.417%. The 30-year bond is up at 104-15/32 to yield 4.477%. June bunds are unchanged at 121.17 and June gilts are down 0.10 at 116.83. (neelabh.chaturvedi@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0834 GMT [Dow Jones] Gilts fall after stronger than expected UK services PMI data. The services PMI for March prints at 57.1 vs expectations for a reading of 52.6. June gilts are down 0.20 at 116.73. (neelabh.chaturvedi@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0824 GMT [Dow Jones] EUR/USD has shown minimal reaction to the run of March Services PMIs which culminating with the final euro zone print being revised up to a 3 1/2 year high of 57.2 from the 56.9 flash. EUR/USD now trades at 1.4182 from 1.4185 when the Spanish PMI hit the wires almost one hour ago. (gary.stride@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0822 GMT [Dow Jones] The USD/MYR is a tad higher at 3.0270 vs 3.0254 in late Asian trade Monday, tracking a slightly weaker SGD, a local dealer says. He adds the 3.0250 level is a strong support as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been suspected of buying dollars at that level over the past few sessions. The pair is expected to continue tracking the SGD in the absence of any local leads. The dealer tips 3.0250-3.0300 range for Wednesday, and activity is likely to be thin as traders will likely be sidelined as Bank Negara is set to keep \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up the pair near the 3.0250 support. (ankur.reliaQ@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0813 GMT [Dow Jones] The willingness of Poland's Monetary Policy Council to tighten policy is boosted by an April inflation expectation reading, which jumped to 4.6% year-on-year from 3.2% in March, says Citi Handlowy. The ratio of inflation expectations to lagged current inflation increased to 1.2, which is the highest outcome since January 2008, when there was still high demand pressure in the economy, Citi says. A similar level was recorded also in September 2010, when the government announced the introduction of VAT tax increases starting from 2011. Bigger ratios were recorded only before Poland joined the EU, when Polish consumers made heavy purchases a few months before EU entry amid concerns over increases in prices. (marynia.kruk@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0803 GMT [Dow Jones] PLN edges up, in thin tade, as investors await the Polish Monetary Policy Council's monthly rate decision, says Karol Zaluski, Chief Foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Dealer at ING in Warsaw. A majority of analysts expect the council to raise rates by 25 basis points today. The EUR/PLN is seen in a wide, 3.97-4.08 range Tuesday, but is expected to move sharply higher if the council fails to deliver the increase, Zaluski says. EUR/PLN at 4.0230 from 4.0325 at mid-day Monday. USD/PLN at 2.8347 from 2.8395. (marynia.kruk@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0801 GMT [Dow Jones] Poland's Monetary Policy Council is likely to raise interest rates by 25 basis points to 4.00% at its Tuesday meeting, says Nordea bank. The decision is expected some time in the afternoon. Following the decision, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Marek Belk is likely to say "that more tightening may come, but not much more and certainly not at every meeting," Nordea says. But the bank says it would not agree with the governor on that point. "Much more tightening will be needed," the bank says. Including the expected April increase as well as the January 25 basis point increase, Nordea sees rates being 125 basis points higher by the end of 2011, versus a year earlier. (marynia.kruk@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0747 GMT [Dow Jones] Portuguese government bonds have largely taken the latest downgrade by \uc2 Moody's\uc2  in their stride for now, with yields stable across the curve with the exception of the 5-year bond where the yield is 2.5 bps higher at 9.808%. \uc2 Moody's\uc2  cut Portugal's rating to Baa1 from A3; Fitch and S&P had cut the country's debt rating last week. The 10-year Portugal/Germany yield spread is stable at 528bps, with the 10-year Portuguese yield at 8.654%. Elsewhere in the periphery, the 10-year Spanish/German yield spread is stable at 190bps while Italy is also unchanged at 148bps. (neelabh.chaturvedi@dowjones.com) [ 04-05-11 0518ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020110405e74500057\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
