fining margins, and as a result of the magnitude-9.0 earthquake and tsunami taking offline almost a quarter of Japan's refining capacity. They plan to run about 2.485 million barrels a day of crude in April, about 45,000 barrels a day more than this month, a Dow Jones Newswires refinery survey shows. South Korea's complex refining margin to benchmark Dubai crude rose to $9.78 a barrel in the week to March 17, up $2.06 from $7.72 a barrel a month earlier, according to Dow Jones Newswires calculations. See REFINERY WATCH: S Korea April Runs Up; Japan Imports, High Margins (wayne.ma@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0924 GMT [Dow Jones] The dollar was mostly lower early in European trading Tuesday, while the euro gained ground after Monday's agreement by E.U. finance ministers on the details of a EUR500B rescue fund to become operative in July 2013. Elsewhere, sterling hit its highest level against the dollar since Jan 2010 ahead of key U.K. inflation data due at 0930 GMT. EUR/USD up at 1.4239, USD/JPY up at 81.077, GBP/USD up at 1.6327. (clare.connaghan@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0924 GMT [Dow Jones] Indonesian shares ended flat at 3517.721, with selling in most commodity-related stocks offsetting gains in select blue chip banks, traders say. They expect the market to consolidate tomorrow amid an absence of fresh leads, and lingering concerns over the situation in Libya. "I think the main index may move in a narrow range of 3500-3550 tomorrow reflecting investors' caution," says a fund manager with a local securities firm. Foreigners were net sellers of IDR227 billion worth of shares. Among decliners: coal producer Bumi (BUMI.JK) ended down 1.6% at IDR3,025, rival Adaro (ADRO.JK) ended down 4.3% at IDR2,225, while nickel miner Inco (INCO.JK) ended down 1.1% at IDR4,650. Bucking the trend, Bank Rakyat (BBRI.JK) finished up 2.0% at IDR5,200 on hopes for strong 2010 earnings to be announced later this week.(edhi.pranasidhi@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0920 GMT [Dow Jones] The 