\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: USD/IDR Higher; 8,770-8,800 Band Tipped Friday\b0\par\par\uc2 1,576 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 10:52\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in Singapore. 65 64154 140; MarketTalk@dowjones.com \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0952 GMT [Dow Jones] The USD/IDR is higher at 8,795 from 8,780 late Wednesday on growing concerns over Japanese nuclear troubles, but is off of its intraday high of 8,805 on suspected \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . Two dealers say Bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  likely sold $150-$200 million around 8,800 to slow the greenback's rise. "More local investors are seeking the U.S. dollar, although volume remains mild so far," says one dealer. He tips the pair to come in a 8,770-8,800 range Friday. (andreasismar.sandiwan@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 0951 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/INR forward premia are lower as call rates eased from early session highs and global crude oil prices are lower, says a trader at a privately-run bank. He adds, "the market had factored in a 25bp hike and the RBI view on anti-inflationary stance may not impact immediately." The one-year premia are at 2.690 from 2.775 late Wednesday. He tips the one-year premia to remain in a 2.68-2.72 band for rest of the session. The overnight call rates are now at 7.65%, off an intraday high of 7.90%. Lower oil prices indicate an easing in inflationary pressure as India imports about 80% of its crude oil needs. (sourav.mishra@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0949 GMT [Dow Jones]--ING doesn't expect an SNB rate hike before September. The Swiss franc's strong appreciation is a useful tool for the SNB in that it curbs the impact on Swiss prices from higher oil prices, and in a small open economy like Switzerland's, it basically works as a monetary tightening, ING economist Julien Manceaux says. "And as consumers are reacting slowly to the recent rise in employment, the SNB seems to think that the Swiss economy has enough monetary tightening for the time being," Manceaux says. (katharina.bart@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0948 GMT [Dow Jones] Thai shares end 0.6% lower at 1002.35 in tandem with losses in most regional bourses; trade is moderate. Lingering concerns over Japan's unfolding nuclear crisis are weighing on market sentiment. "As long as Japan's problem remains in focus, the (Thai) stock market direction will track regional markets," says Capital Nomura Securities Chai Jirasevenupraphund. He tips support at 995-990 and resistance at 1010. Among the most active shares, PTT (PTT.TH) is down 0.9% at THB336, Banpu (BANPU.TH) is off 0.5% at THB738, IRPC (IRPC.TH) is flat at THB6.0, \uc2 Indorama Ventures\uc2  (IVL.TH) is off 1.0% at THB49.25 and \uc2 Charoen Pokphand Foods\uc2  (CPF.TH) is up 0.4% at THB25. (oranan.paweewun@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0945 GMT [Dow Jones--The SNB is leaving all its options open in terms of when and how to raise interest rates, says Hyposwiss's Thomas Stucki. "The SNB has been quite clever in that on the one hand, they highlight the strong economic picture, but on the other hand they have put the strong Swiss franc very much in focus too. They are leaving all their options open in terms of hiking rates," Stucki says. His forecasts call for a 25-basis-point hike in September. (katharina.bart@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0942 GMT [Dow Jones] The Sensex extends losses, down 1.3% at 18,117.39, after the RBI raises policy rates by 25 bps each and increases its March-end inflation forecast to 8% from 7%. "The rate hike was along expected lines, but the increase in the inflation forecast is not an encouraging sign," says a local dealer. He adds, the RBI has said it will stick to an anti-inflationary stance and that means further rate hikes are likely in coming months. \uc2 Maruti Suzuki India\uc2  (532500.BY) is down 4.6% at INR1,167.30 due to concerns the recent sharp rise in the JPY will push up the company's import costs. \uc2 Housing Development Finance Corp\uc2 . (500010.BY) is down 4.0% at INR635.00, while \uc2 Reliance Industries\uc2  (500325.BY) is 1.5% lower at INR1,028.50. Among gainers, \uc2 Bharat Heavy Electricals\uc2  (500103.BY) is 1.9% higher at INR1,962.00. A Dow Jones technical analyst tips the Sensex in a 18,050-18,500 range for the rest of the session. (sudeep.jain@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0941 GMT [Dow Jones] The zloty is down and could weaken further Thursday, as the Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains a proxy for the region, a dealer says. "The zloty is still reacting more violently than other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to any negative global threat," he says. "Newsflow from Japan remains in focus, while the EUR/PLN is seen in a 4.07-4.11 range today." He adds that the end of the week will give some indication of whether this zloty weakening is the beginning of a larger cycle or whether it will play itself out. EUR/PLN now trades at 4.0862 from 4.0458 Wednesday. USD/PLN at 2.9205 from 2.8966. (marynia.kruk@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0940 GMT [Dow Jones] India interbank call rates are off their highs but continue to remain at elevated levels as system liquidity moves into sharp deficit due to advance tax outflows, says a dealer with a state-run bank. The overnight call rates are now at 7.65% versus an intraday high of 7.90%. "Apart from advance tax, there is also a rush among branches to disburse sanctioned loans before the end of the fiscal year on March 31, which is keeping demand for cash high," he says. He expects the call rates to remain in a 7.50%-8.00% band in the near term, above the RBI's repo rate of 6.75%. The RBI says in its mid-quarter review of monetary policy that liquidity may come under some temporary pressure in the second half of March due to advance tax collections. It however disclose whether it will extend the additional liquidity easing steps--holding a second daily liquidity auction and allowing banks to borrow to an extent of 1% of deposits--which are to expire on April 8. (nupur.acharya@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0938 GMT [Dow Jones] Pakistan shares trade a tad higher, supported by gains in oil and fertilizer stocks. The benchmark KSE-100 index is up 0.1% at 11,800.58. "Some buying from local financial institutions, mainly in oil and fertilizer plays, are helping the index to stay afloat," says a domestic dealer. He adds, volume is modest as uncertainty in regional markets on the Japan disaster and ongoing crises in the Middle East are keeping sentiment subdued. Foreign funds sold shares worth $2.9 million Wednesday. He says, "the market outlook appears to be depressed as the government has imposed a 15% flood surcharge on income tax of companies, which would crimp earnings of blue chips." He tips the index in a 11,600-11,900 range in the near term. \uc2 Pakistan State Oil\uc2  (PSO.KA) is up 0.4% at PKR280.01 and \uc2 Engro Corp\uc2 . (ENGRO.KA) is up 1.0% at PKR195.75. (djn.in@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0938 GMT [Dow Jones] Russian capital outflows are due to surplus capital arriving in the country from high oil prices but not being absorbed by the economy, \uc2 UniCredit\uc2  says. "We think the main reason for the continued capital flight is relatively loose monetary policy on top of persistent weak investment demand in Russia, which keeps interest rates low and capital away from the country." Russia has seen around $17B in outflows so far this year, almost half of what it saw in all of 2010. (ira.iosebashvili@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0937 GMT [Dow Jones] Thai government bonds are higher on lingering worries over the nuclear crisis in Japan. Offshore participants are seen buying, especially long-dated notes. However, "some local players took profit after the recent rally, bringing yields off their lows," says a bond trader. The focus is on how Japan's situation evolves for potential trading cues. Without any fresh factors, yields are expected to remain rangebound in the near-term. The bid/offer yield of bonds due December 2015 are quoted at 3.29%/3.25% from 3.32%/3.30% in late Asian trade Wednesday, the October 2017 yield is at 3.55%/3.50% from 3.60%/3.50% and the December 2021 yield is at 3.75%/3.70% from 3.84%/3.82%. (phisanu.phromchanya@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0936 GMT [Dow Jones] The USD/THB weakens to 30.32-30.33 from 30.41-30.42 late Wednesday in Asia, bucking the regional trend with some exporters seen selling, a Bangkok-based dealer says; trade is moderate. "It seems that liquidity is low and for some reason, with the USD/JPY down a lot, it is having an impact on the USD/THB," he says; he adds, overall, the market remains fairly directionless despite the THB strength. He expects the pair may break through 30.30 Friday, after which it could shift down quickly to 30.25, although the \uc2 Bank of Thailand\uc2  may step in around that level to stem the pace of the downside. Resistance is tipped at 30.35. (leigh.murray@dowjones.com) [ 03-17-11 0552ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020110317e73h0006t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
