l trading cues. The Market has widely priced in a 25-bp hike, with a few expecting a 50-bps move. Yields are expected to stay in tight ranges early next week. The bid/offer yield of bonds due December 2015 are quoted at 3.40%/3.39% from 3.44%/3.41% late Thursday, the October 2017 yield is bid at 3.62%/3.54% from 3.62%/3.58% and the December 2021 yield is at 3.95%/3.93% from 3.95%/3.90%. (phisanu.phromchanya@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0920 GMT [Dow Jones] \uc2 RBC Capital Markets\uc2  expects the ECB to raise its refinancing rate by 75 bps this year, while the 10-year bund yield is likely to climb to 3.60% in 4Q; the bund is currently at 3.30%. "This rather moderate rate increase profile coupled with a rather benign outlook for U.S. Treasurys should keep bund yields from rising substantially," RBC says. RBC also expects gilts to outperform bunds as budget adjustments find their way into tighter swap spreads before BOE starts raising rates. (neelabh.chaturvedi@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0919 GMT [Dow Jones] GBP/USD has posted a bearish divergence warning and measures of trend are still pointed lower, says \uc2 Barclays Capital\uc2 . Now at 1.6240, the bank sees immediate risk toward support at 1.6215, with a break here targeting the 1.61 area. However, for the bigger picture, BarCap prefers to buy such a pullback if seen to position for a move to the January 2010 high of 1.6460. (gary.stride@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0917 GMT [Dow Jones] The KLCI ends 1.0% higher at 1522.61 on gains across the board, in line with regional bourses following a strong showing on Wall Street Thursday. Gains were led by plantation and construction stocks. However, a local dealer says that trading volumes, which have been thinner than usual, indicate that players remain cautious; "frankly we're surprised the market hasn't succumbed to profit-taking by now... with so much uncertainty over high oil prices and the turmoil in the Middle East, investors are taking a very short-term view of the market," the dealer says. He tips a 1500-1530 range for Monday. Market breadth is positive with 674 advancers compared with 148 decliners. Among advancers \uc2 KL Kepong\uc2  (2445.KU) ended up 2.9% at MYR21.10, Genting (3182.KU) ended 3.2% higher at MYR10.34, \uc2 IOI Corp\uc2  (1961.KU) ended up 2.9% at MYR5.73 and WCT (9679.KU) ended 3.0% higher at MYR3.09. Among decliners Proton (5304.KU) ended down 5.2% at MYR3.27 and BAT (4162.KU) ended 1.3% lower at MYR48.10. (kwan-por.lee@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0912 GMT [Dow Jones] India's short-end overnight indexed swaps are slightly down as some concern the RBI will take rate action at the March 17 rate setting meeting ebbs as a liquidity crunch eases and as weekly price food inflation slows, says a trader at a privately-run bank. One-year OIS are at 7.40%/7.42% from 7.42%/7.44% late Thursday. Five-year OIS are at 8.00%/8.02% from 8.02%/8.04%. "The liquidity is improving significantly, which is good for the short-end. Some government spending is trickling down to the system," the trader says. He tips the one-year OIS in a 7.40%-7.45% band for the session. Indian banks borrowed INR318.35 billion from the RBI at the first repo window so far in the session. The average daily borrowing has come down to between INR600 billion-INR800 billion this week from about INR1 trillion in the previous week. For the week to Feb. 19, the on-year inflation rate for food articles eased to 10.39% from 11.49% a week earlier. (sourav.mishra@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0910 GMT [Dow Jones] The USD/TWD is down late at 29.4620 from 29.5420 late Thursday on the back of Taiex strength and USD weakness, a local trader says. "Right now the U.S. dollar is very weak, so many (market participants) are waiting to see if Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  will continue to rise," in which case foreign investors are likely to continue selling next week, he says. He tips pair to test as low as 29.3000 on Monday, adding that there is strong support at the psychological 29.0000 level. (paul.mozur@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0908 GMT [Dow Jones] Recent flattening saw the UK 2/10-year curve flatten to around 213bps, generating an oversold condition, according to Nomura. They see the spread widening back out to 243 bps over the next couple of weeks, the "steep" side of its recent 213-243 bps trading range, before flattening again and attempting to make a new low. The 2/10-year gilt yield spread is currently 234 bps. (nick.cawley@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0906 GMT [Dow Jones] The USD/PHP settles lower late, in line with the USD's weakness against the EUR and regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , prompting the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , two local bank traders say. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have bought around $200 million between 43.25-43.27 shortly before the session close in a bid to temper the PHP's rise, traders say. One trader says higher-than-expected inflation of 4.3% in February was also lifting the PHP. The pair settles at 43.28, marking its lowest in close to four months, from 43.36 late Thursday amid heavy trading. Traders tip the pair within a 43.20-43.50 range Monday as participants are likely to look for cues from overseas. (rhea.sandique-carlos@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0904 GMT [Dow Jones] Pakistan shares are higher, led by oil stocks. The benchmark KSE-100 index is up 1.6% at 11,992.31. "Buying from local investors is dominating the proceedings following the stock market regulator's move to resume 'Market Trading System' - allowing investors to buy shares on borrowed money," says a dealer with a domestic brokerage. He adds, the new facility will be available soon as the finance minister, Hafeez Shaikh, is to officially introduce it from Saturday to improve liquidity. The continuous funding system, commonly known as badla, was halted in 2008 when several investors took long positions and were unable to square them off. He says the new product will improve the daily business volume, which averages around 90 million shares now. Before 2008, volumes were around 300 million shares. The dealer expects the index to face resistance at 12,080. \uc2 Pakistan State Oil\uc2  (PSO.KA) is up 4.0% at PKR290.50 and Oil & Gas Development (OGDC.KA) is up 1.0% at PKR153.20. (djn.in@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0850 GMT [Dow Jones] Core euro-zone bond spreads are flat to a fraction wider in early Friday trade as investors calculate the effect of higher ECB rates. Outright yields on most countries are higher after Thursday's bund sell-off with Portugal's 10-year now yielding 7.42%, nearing the level of the last round of ECB \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , while its 2-year spread is 8 bps wider at 398 bps. Spanish spreads are wider by a couple of bps on the back of yesterday's 3- and 5-year auctions. (nick.cawley@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0835 GMT [Dow Jones] The zloty should recover slightly Friday, expected to take advantage of higher risk appetite, says BZ WBK. The bank sees first support for EUR/PLN at 3.984, second at 3.976. The resistance for EUR/PLN is seen at 4.00. EUR/PLN now trades at 3.9940. (malgorzata.halaba@dowjones.com) [ 03-04-11 0424ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020110304e73400054\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
