\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: USD/IDR Flat; 8,800-8,820 Band Tipped Wednesday\b0\par\par\uc2 1,353 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 11:06\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in Singapore. 65 64154 140; MarketTalk@dowjones.com \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1006 GMT [Dow Jones] The USD/IDR is flat at 8,810 late, off an intraday high of 8,815; the pair may continue to fall in the near term as Bank Indonesia allows the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to appreciate faster in its bid to lower imported inflation, dealers say. But ING says further rises by the IDR are likely to be limited this week after it gained 2.6% in February. The house tips the pair to target 8,750 within the next three months. "The rupiah is still in a strengthening trend," says a local dealer, but he expects Bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  near the 8,800 level to avoid IDR from rising too fast. He tips the pair in a 8,800-8,820 range Wednesday. (andreasismar.sandiwan@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 0952 GMT [Dow Jones] With the USD index at fresh 2011 lows, \uc2 Barclays Capital\uc2  says the risk of a EUR/USD pullback to 1.3610 has diminished. Now at 1.3826, the bank says a break above the recent high of 1.3865 will confirm the move in the USD index, and resume the uptrend in EUR/USD toward 1.40. EUR/USD now at 1.3820, the USD index trades at 76.862. (gary.stride@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0950 GMT [Dow Jones] Thai shares end up 0.7% at 994.48 in tandem with gains in regional bourses; trade is moderate. Banking stocks are buoyant as they are laggards in the Thai market's recent rally. "However, further upside (in Thai shares) is likely limited as concerns over political tensions in the Middle East still linger," says SCB Securities Senior Vice President Sukit Udomsirikul. He tips near-term resistance at 995 and then 1000, and support at 985. Among the most active shares, TMB Bank (TMB.TH) surges 4.4% to THB2.38, Banpu (BANPU.TH) is flat at THB726, \uc2 Kasikornbank\uc2  (KBANK.TH) is up 1.7% at THB119.50 and \uc2 Siam Commercial Bank\uc2  (SCB.TH) rises 1.0% to THB103. Bucking the trend, \uc2 Charoen Pokphand Foods\uc2  (CPF.TH) is down 0.8% at THB23.60. (oranan.paweewun@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0950 GMT [Dow Jones] Switch from ICO's Feb 2015 bonds at swaps +199 bps into FADE's June 2015 issue at swaps +220 bps says \uc2 UniCredit\uc2 . Both issuers are Spanish agencies that benefit from guarantees from the Kingdom of Spain, and thus "fundamentally... should trade at a similar level." ICO is in the market with a 10-year deal Tuesday, at 75-80 bps over the Spanish government bond curve. (mark.brown@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0948 GMT [Dow Jones] European sovereign debt insurance costs fall Tuesday, data provider Markit says, as a rally in the credit and equity markets gains momentum. Spain's 5-year CDS spread is 8 bps tighter at 247 bps, Portugal 5 bps tighter at 460 and Italy 5 bps tighter at 175, Markit says. Notes CDS for Ireland is 9 bps tighter at 570 bps, with Belgium 6 bps tighter at 167. The financial indexes are moving in the same way, with the Senior Financials index 4.5 bps tighter at 151.5 and the Subordinated Financials index 5 bps tighter at 260, Markit says. (hannah.benjamin@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0947 GMT [Dow Jones] Thai government bonds are barely changed in very thin trade, shrugging off the February CPI data, which rose 2.87% on year and expanded 0.4% on month. February core CPI was up 1.45% on year and rose 0.14% on month. "The market is aware that interest rates are on the rise, but investors are not actively making any move. Most of them are sticking with the short-dated tenors for the sake of liquidity," says a local dealer. She adds, the yields are likely to be steady, although eyes are on the auction results of MOF's bond worth THB7 billion due December 2021 Wednesday. The bid/offer yield of bonds due December 2015 are quoted at 3.39%/3.37% from 3.40%/3.36% late Monday, the October 2017 yield is at 3.60%/3.55% from 3.62%/3.55% and the December 2021 yield is at 3.97%/3.94% from 3.96%/3.90%. (piyarat.setthasiriphaiboon@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0944 GMT [Dow Jones] Gilts are down on the day, but stable after a stronger-than-expected reading of UK manufacturing PMI. The manufacturing PMI printed at 61.5 in February vs expectations for a reading of 61.1. June gilts are down 0.24 at 116.45. (neelabh.chaturvedi@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0943 GMT [Dow Jones] The USD/THB is nearly flat at 30.57-30.58 from 30.570 late Monday after moderate trade. Most transactions are trade-related, with only a handful for investment flows, says Bangkok-based dealer. "The dollar/baht will likely stick within a fairly tight range until the BOT's policy meeting" on March 9, she says. Investors are awaiting testimony by Fed Chairman Bernanke to the U.S. Senate Banking Committee later in the global day for potential trading cues. Dollar demand from Japanese firms ahead of the Japanese fiscal-year book-closing later this month is likely to limit the pair's downside, while exporters' sale orders at 30.60 and above will likely cap any upside. The pair is tipped in a 30.55-30.62 range in the near-term. (phisanu.phromchanya@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0942 GMT [Dow Jones] The USD/PKR is down at 85.67 late Tuesday from 85.70 late Monday; "the dollar rose to 85.72 during the day, but sales by exporters attracted by the high levels pulled it back," says a dealer. However, the pair is expected to bounce back, helped by rising crude oil prices, which are increasing the country's import bill, he adds. He tips the pair in a 85.65-85.75 range Wednesday. (djn.in@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0939 GMT [Dow Jones] Only small gains for sterling despite the fact that at 61.5 the February UK manufacturing PMI not only beat expectations but was also an all-time high. GBP/USD trades at 1.6305 while EUR/GBP is just a couple of ticks lower at 0.8478. (gary.stride@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0938 GMT [Dow Jones] China onshore IRS rebound on bargain hunting after falling for more than a week. One-year IRS are up 2 bps at 3.71%-3.80% after falling 26 bps since Feb. 21. Five-year IRS are up 5 bps at 4.20%-4.29% after losing 29 bps in the same period. "The focus is back on inflation again. No matter how the upheaval in the Middle East and North Africa evolves, China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  still needs to hike interest rates to curb inflation," says a Shanghai-based foreign bank trader, who tips IRS are generally trending higher. Higher interest rates are likely to boost IRS. (wynne.wang@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0934 GMT [Dow Jones] Indonesian shares end up 1.2% at 3512.617 in moderate volume, helped by hopes the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will leave its key interest rate unchanged at 6.75% at its policy meeting Friday after benign inflation data for February, traders say. They expect the market to extend gains Wednesday on further bargain buying, tipping the main index to top 3550. The main index is still down 5.2% since the start of 2011. "The firmer rupiah and gains across Asian markets due to lower crude oil prices also improved sentiment on the local bourse," says a trader with Erdhika Securities. Foreigners were net buyers of IDR570 billion worth of shares. Among interest-rate sensitive stocks, Bank Rakyat (BBRI.JK) is +4.3% at IDR4,900, Bank Negara (BBNI.JK) is +2.1% at IDR3,625 and carmaker Astra (ASII.JK) is +3.8% at IDR54,000. (edhi.pranasidhi@dowjones.com) [ 03-01-11 0506ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020110301e7310006n\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
