\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Indonesia eyes fuel subsidy cut delay, to let rupiah rise\b0\par\par\uc2 567 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Februar 2011\par 06:40\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds details)\par \par \uc2 JAKARTA, Feb 24 (Reuters) - Indonesia said on Thursday it is considering delaying a plan to limit the use of cheap subsidised fuels to next year as it seeks to avoid surging oil prices adding to inflation, despite a potential cost of over $600 million to the state budget.\par \par \uc2 Chief economics minister Hatta Rajasa said the government has no plans to hike subsidised fuel prices, a move that would boost inflation and likely to lead to protests. Vietnam on Thursday hiked gasoline and diesel prices by up to 24 percent.\par \par \uc2 Instead, Indonesia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will let the rupiah \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strengthen to curb imported inflation, deputy governor Hartadi A. Sarwono said, as it is concerned about high oil prices following turmoil in the Middle East.\par \par \uc2 Indonesia's government had aimed to stop private cars in the capital Jakarta from using cheap subsidised fuel from end-March, before rolling the pan out across the country, but may delay the start, said Rajasa.\par \par \uc2 "The financial consequences would be to add 3-6 trillion rupiah of additional subsidies for one year," said finance minister Agus Martowardojo.\par \par \uc2 The comments come as London oil prices surged over $6 to $117 a barrel, and ahead of Indonesia's February's inflation data next Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Some analysts see higher-than-expected inflation leading Bank Indonesia to hike rates by another 25 basis points when meeting on March 4 in an effort to stem price pressures, after January inflation reached a 21-month-high of 7 percent.\par \par \uc2 "We are concerned over imported inflation both from oil and food prices. We keep monitoring rising oil prices," Bank Indonesia's Sarwono told reporters.\par \par \uc2 Sarwono said Indonesia's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves had reached a record $97 billion, a level nearly double two years ago and that gives the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  more ammunition to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2 Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  hiked rates by 150 basis points in 2008 to counter growing inflation after the government was forced to hike subsidised fuel prices by almost 30 percent on average because of record oil prices.\par \par \uc2 Indonesia is the country in Southeast Asia that is the most exposed to a sharp rise in oil prices and policymakers will face a dilemma as tightening rates may slow growth, CIMB said in a report on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 "Some central banks are willing to tolerate a stronger \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as part of their efforts to bring inflation under control," said CIMB's Lee Heng Guie.\par \par \uc2 The rupiah has gained 1.5 percent this year, adding to near 5 percent gains last year.\par \par \uc2 The former OPEC oil producer is forced to import gasoline and diesel from the regional market since its ageing refineries do not produce enough fuel, but still maintains subsidised fuel.\par \par \uc2 Analysts say the government needs to use the money spent on subsidies to instead improve infrastructure, which would help draw further foreign direct investment and improve the chances of getting a coveted investment grade sovereign rating.\par \par \uc2 However, protests over price hikes were seen as a major factor in the ousting of Indonesia's autocratic President Suharto in 1998 and would hit the current administration's popularity. (Reporting by Adriana Nina Kusuma, Rieka Rahadiana and Aditya Suharmoko; Editing by Neil Chatterjee)\par \par \uc2 INDONESIA-ECONOMY/INFLATION (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|D|E|RBN|IF|M|O|OIL|RNP|DNP|PTD|PEN   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110224e72o000mi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw442\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6630\pichgoal600
