ight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Thus, the recent correction in local stock market and the Hong Kong dollar is only temporary." He tips the pair to trade between 7.7830 and 7.7860 band today. (fiona.law@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0146 GMT [Dow Jones] China's first interest rate hike in 2011 could come around the Lunar New Year holiday in early February, state-run China Securities Journal said in a commentary Friday without citing sources. The paper said that strong inflation pressure could push the consumer price index to exceed 6.0% during part of 1H. The paper also said Beijing will continue to raise the reserve requirement ratio for banks, and allow the yuan to appreciate to help lower the price of imported goods. China Securities Journal is a paper designated for disclosing securities news under the Xinhua News Agency instead of through the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Although the paper didn't cite any sources, the report comes at a time when investors are concerned that China's inflation could pick up further. (wynne.wang@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0144 GMT [Dow Jones] Singapore's STI rises 0.1% to 3208.47 after a weaker open, with bearish regional cues tussling with a resilient Wall Street session Thursday and also on some buying back after yesterday's 1.1% drop. STI components are evenly mixed, with declines in banks and gains in property names. The broad market is also evenly matched, with 244 million shares traded worth S$196 million. After overnight losses for crude oil and copper, Phillip Securities says the commodity market "is suggesting risk-off at this point" and that it might be "further evidence of unwinding of emerging market positions and going long U.S. equities again." For the STI, it says short-term RSI conditions are currently oversold due to yesterday's sharp sell down; it also says minor resistance is at 3213 before 3220, a rejection of which "would be very bearish." Support at 3190/3185 then 3170. ST Engine