\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: USD/TWD Tad Higher; 29.100-29.150 Band Tipped\b0\par\par\uc2 1,634 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Januar 2011\par 03:22\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in Singapore. 65 64154 140; \par MarketTalk@dowjones.com \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0222 GMT [Dow Jones] The USD/TWD is at 29.126, up from a trading band of 29.025-29.050 yesterday, as some foreign investors start to buy amid falling local stocks, says a local trader. "Some foreign investors found that the New Taiwan dollar has strong resistance at NT$29.000 against the U.S. dollar...and they don't want to park their money here too long, especially as the Lunar New Year holidays are approaching." He adds the pair's direction is likely to be affected by the performance of local stocks in the near term (the Taiex is last down 0.8%). He tips the pair to trade in a 29.100-29.150 band for the session. (fanny.liu@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 0222 GMT [Dow Jones] Volatilities implied by one-month at-the-money USD/JPY options are unchanged from late Thursday in New York at 9.70%/10.40% as the USD/JPY remains in a narrow 82.86-83.09 range in spot trading, says a senior dealer at a major Japanese bank. He expects the pair to be rangebound for the rest of the session, fenced in by exporters' selling and speculators' buying. He adds, volatilities are likely to start falling as investors may start selling toward the weekend. (takashi.mochizuki@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0222 GMT [Dow Jones] Crude oil futures are a tad lower in early Asia trade on a bearish inventory report late Thursday and amid concerns of further monetary policy tightening by China; although previous measures by Beijing haven't slowed oil demand, interest rate hikes have had a S/T bearish impact on crude; a report that another hike may be only weeks away will weigh on sentiment. Weaker re