ll their stocks (to lock in profits) before the upcoming Lunar New Year holidays." But he adds, the rebound in China stock markets today as well as some local tech shares such as \uc2 Largan Precision\uc2  (3008.TW) is providing some support. He tips the Taiex to find initial support at its 30-day moving average around 8930, with next support at 8900; he adds, resistance is pegged at 9000. TSMC (2330.TW) is down 1.8% at NT$74.90, UMC (2303.TW) is down 0.6% at NT$17.55, and \uc2 AU Optronics\uc2  (2409.TW) is down 1.7% at NT$28.60. \uc2 Largan Precision\uc2  is up 0.4% at NT$774. (fanny.liu@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0214 GMT [Dow Jones] The USD/KRW is lurching in and out of gains amid a lack of any strong one-sided momentum; the pair is nearly flat at 1,121.50 from 1,121.20 late Thursday in Seoul. Traders note upward momentum for the pair isn't very strong despite concerns over further monetary policy tightening by China ahead of the weekend; "I don't see the kind of (strong) short dollar covering by offshore players we saw yesterday," helping the pair retreat a bit, says a local bank trader, who expects the pair to test 1,120 support. Exporters aren't selling much in the morning session, but if they sell USD in bigger volumes in the afternoon, the pair may slip below 1,120. (min-jeong.lee@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0213 GMT [Dow Jones] The USD/PHP is falling as banks start to unload some long USD positions. The pair is last quoted at 44.42 in moderate volume after settling late yesterday at 44.50 and spiking to 44.61 earlier today. Traders peg support at 44.30. "It seems a lot of banks were caught long, so they're easing up on those positions. We haven't seen the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  so far," says a local bank trader. (cris.larano@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0211 GMT [Dow Jones] The USD/CNY is higher, tracking gains in the USD index. Friday's central parity is set at 6.5886, slightly higher than Thursday's record low of 6.5883, indi