\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK:Indonesia Shares End Down 2.3%;3440 Support Tipped\b0\par\par\uc2 1,238 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Januar 2011\par 10:28\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in Singapore. 65 64154 140; \par MarketTalk@dowjones.com \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0928 GMT [Dow Jones] Indonesia shares end down 2.3% at 3454.118 in moderate volume, weighed by inflation concerns, a weak rupiah and falls across Asian markets, traders say. They expect the market continue to fall ahead of the weekend and amid an absence of fresh leads from the domestic economy, tipping support at 3440. "Selloff in most commodity and consumer-related stocks weighed down overall sentiment here despite sporadic buying by some local institutional funds," says a trader with a foreign securities firm. Foreigners are net sellers of IDR38 billion worth of shares. Among decliners, coal producer Adaro (ADRO.JK) is down 7.6% at IDR2,450 on hopes for weak full year earnings, rival Bumi (BUMI.JK) is down 3.2% at IDR3,050, while Bank Negara (BBNI.JK) is down 3.7% at IDR3,225 on profit-taking. (edhi.pranasidhi@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 0927 GMT [Dow Jones] The zloty is edging down as investors who had bet Poland's Monetary Policy Council would raise rates at its January sitting take profit after the long-awaited increase materialized Wednesday, a dealer says. EUR/PLN could inch up some more, but 3.91 is a strong ceiling, he adds. EUR/PLN trades at 3.8896 from 3.8749 late Tuesday, USD/PLN at 2.8840 from 2.8710. Average yield on 2-year bonds is at 4.95% from 4.93% late Wednesday, while 5-year is unchanged at 5.73%. Average yield on 10-year bonds is at 6.28% from 6.31%. (marynia.kruk@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0922 GMT [Dow Jones] The USD/IDR is higher at 9,068 vs 9,055 late yesterday, tracking USD gains against several Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and also on foreign selling of bonds and local stocks. But the pair is off its intraday high of 9,075, on suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , say three dealers. "Foreigners are cutting their holdings especially in bonds, and BI seems to be keeping the pair in a narrow band to avoid volatility," a senior dealer at foreign bank says. He adds, the IDR may face heavy selling pressure near-term on inflation risks, and tips the pair to trade in a 9,050-9,100 range Friday. (andreasismar.sandiwan@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0920 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/ZAR hits a fresh 7-week high of 7.0247 Thursday ahead of the Reserve Bank's interest rate decision where rates are expected to be left on hold at 5.5%. \uc2 Citigroup\uc2  trader Julian Wilson say there are several factors behind the move include buying by oil importers, foreign selling of government bonds and general unwinding of long positions since the end of the year. (mariam.isa@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0917 GMT [Dow Jones] The USD/THB rises to 30.55 from 30.47-30.49 in thin trade, tracking broader dollar gains against Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The pair moved in a tight range amid the absence of fresh drivers. "Most activity is just to square positions...the directionless trend is likely to continue on Friday," says a local dealer. Although the market has already priced in the overall economic outlook of Thailand this year, the quarterly economic forecast by the \uc2 Bank of Thailand\uc2  scheduled Friday is still a factor to watch. He tips support at 30.46 and resistance at 30.62. (piyarat.setthasiriphaiboon@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0917 GMT [Dow Jones] SEB says the market has spent the week digesting the EUR/SEK surge a week ago and "we also continue to point to a second leg higher toward 9.05/10." Notes downside attempts below 8.8900 should only be temporary and if seen, bought. Next resistance seen at 8.9575. EUR/SEK trades at 8.9264. (dominic.chopping@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0916 GMT [Dow Jones] The USD/TWD is at 29.460, compared to 29.450 late yesterday; the pair recouped all its losses late in the session, when two state-owned banks struck a deal at 29.460 after the pair hovered in a 29.025-29.050 band most of the day, two traders say. One of them says some exporters were selling, but not much; he adds, although the local stock market was down today, the overall trend is still up and inflows will likely continue to keep the pair trading below 29.050 near-term. The Taiex ended down 0.7%. (aries.poon@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0913 GMT [Dow Jones] GBP has had a good run recently, and \uc2 Citigroup\uc2  notes hedge fund positioning has become much more balanced over the past month, with positive positioning in decline. "This signals there is significant scope for hedge funds to add to long positions at present," the bank says. GBP/USD trades at 1.5974. (jessica.mead@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0910 GMT [Dow Jones] Pakistan shares trade lower led by oil shares; the benchmark KSE-100 index is down 0.6% at 12,505.31 on profit-taking after recent gains. "Some investors are cashing out after the recent outperformance. Concerns the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will further raise rates at its month-end monetary policy meeting due to high inflation are also keeping investor sentiment subdued," says a dealer. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will meet on Jan. 29. He adds, the index could trade in a 12,400-12,600 range near-term. \uc2 Pakistan State Oil\uc2  (PSO.KA) is down 0.9% at PKR302.50 and Oil & Gas Development (OGDC.KA) is down 0.6% at PKR172.09. (djn.in@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0908 GMT [Dow Jones] March gilt futures are vulnerable while trading below 117.90 and look to test the 116.86/89 level before exposing the market to 115.84, the June 15 low, according to \uc2 UBS\uc2 . March gilt futures trade at 117.19, down 25 ticks on the day.(nick.cawley@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0907 GMT [Dow Jones] HUF gives back some of its marked gains of the past few days as stock markets are down in Europe and as the PLN didn't firm after a rate hike. EUR/HUF is at 272.40 versus two-month record levels of below 272 Tuesday. \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2  says that chances of EUR/HUF dipping below 270 appear slim, but it doesn't rule out increased demand for Hungarian government bonds from international investors ahead of Monday's rate decision as bets for rate hikes are being scaled back. "What we also find interesting is the fact that the Hungarian CDS curve is one of the flattest in the region, which makes us inclined to sell 1-year CDS around 280bp," BNP adds. (margit.feher@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0901 GMT [Dow Jones] The USD/PHP is higher late, taking cues from the EUR's weakness; but the gains are capped on suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in support of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , say 2 dealers. The pair is at 44.50 from 44.26 late Wednesday amid heavy trading. "There was a bit of heavy-buying," says a local bank trader, adding that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have sold around $500 million at the 44.46 level. The trader adds, the pair may stay in a 44.20-44.60 band Friday as the market eyes overseas cues. (rhea.sandique-carlos@dowjones.com) [ 01-20-11 0428ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020110120e71k00062\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
