ly to continue on Friday," says a local dealer. Although the market has already priced in the overall economic outlook of Thailand this year, the quarterly economic forecast by the \uc2 Bank of Thailand\uc2  scheduled Friday is still a factor to watch. He tips support at 30.46 and resistance at 30.62. (piyarat.setthasiriphaiboon@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0917 GMT [Dow Jones] SEB says the market has spent the week digesting the EUR/SEK surge a week ago and "we also continue to point to a second leg higher toward 9.05/10." Notes downside attempts below 8.8900 should only be temporary and if seen, bought. Next resistance seen at 8.9575. EUR/SEK trades at 8.9264. (dominic.chopping@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0916 GMT [Dow Jones] The USD/TWD is at 29.460, compared to 29.450 late yesterday; the pair recouped all its losses late in the session, when two state-owned banks struck a deal at 29.460 after the pair hovered in a 29.025-29.050 band most of the day, two traders say. One of them says some exporters were selling, but not much; he adds, although the local stock market was down today, the overall trend is still up and inflows will likely continue to keep the pair trading below 29.050 near-term. The Taiex ended down 0.7%. (aries.poon@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0913 GMT [Dow Jones] GBP has had a good run recently, and \uc2 Citigroup\uc2  notes hedge fund positioning has become much more balanced over the past month, with positive positioning in decline. "This signals there is significant scope for hedge funds to add to long positions at present," the bank says. GBP/USD trades at 1.5974. (jessica.mead@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0910 GMT [Dow Jones] Pakistan shares trade lower led by oil shares; the benchmark KSE-100 index is down 0.6% at 12,505.31 on profit-taking after recent gains. "Some investors are cashing out after the recent outperformance. Concerns the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will further raise rates at its month-end monetary policy meeting due to high inflation are also keeping investor sentiment subdued," says a dealer. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will meet on Jan. 29. He adds, the index could trade in a 12,400-12,600 range near-term. \uc2 Pakistan State Oil\uc2  (PSO.KA) is down 0.9% at PKR302.50 and Oil & Gas Development (OGDC.KA) is down 0.6% at PKR172.09. (djn.in@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0908 GMT [Dow Jones] March gilt futures are vulnerable while trading below 117.90 and look to test the 116.86/89 level before exposing the market to 115.84, the June 15 low, according to \uc2 UBS\uc2 . March gilt futures trade at 117.19, down 25 ticks on the day.(nick.cawley@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0907 GMT [Dow Jones] HUF gives back some of its marked gains of the past few days as stock markets are down in Europe and as the PLN didn't firm after a rate hike. EUR/HUF is at 272.40 versus two-month record levels of below 272 Tuesday. \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2  says that chances of EUR/HUF dipping below 270 appear slim, but it doesn't rule out increased demand for Hungarian government bonds from international investors ahead of Monday's rate decision as bets for rate hikes are being scaled back. "What we also find interesting is the fact that the Hungarian CDS curve is one of the flattest in the region, which makes us inclined to sell 1-year CDS around 280bp," BNP adds. (margit.feher@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0901 GMT [Dow Jones] The USD/PHP is higher late, taking cues from the EUR's weakness; but the gains are capped on suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in support of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , say 2 dealers. The pair is at 44.50 from 44.26 late Wednesday amid heavy trading. "There was a bit of heavy-buying," says a local bank trader, adding that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have sold around $500 million at the 44.46 level. The trader adds, the pair may stay in a 44.20-44.6